<h1>Likutay Halachos</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Choshen Mishpat &mdash; Laws of Buying and Selling (<em>Mekach Umimkar</em>) 1&ndash;4</p>

<!-- ==================== MEKACH UMIMKAR 1 ==================== -->

<h2>Mekach Umimkar 1</h2>

<div class="halachah-intro">
<strong>Halachic Heading:</strong> Lifting up (<em>hagbahah</em>) acquires in every situation, and it is the most important acquisition of all the acquisitions.
</div>

<p class="no-indent"><em>Based on Likutay Moharan I, Torah 280.</em></p>

<h3>&sect;1</h3>

<p class="no-indent">Based on what is explained in the words of Rabbainu, may his light shine, on the verse <span class="verse">&ldquo;When you go out to war&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan I:280]</span> &mdash; that the aspect of <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> <span class="bracket">[commerce/negotiation]</span> is that one lifts up and raises the thing, and then returns and places it in its proper place. That is, one raises and elevates the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> <span class="bracket">[holy sparks]</span> that are clothed there, for this is the essence of <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> &mdash; to elevate the sparks; see there. And this is accomplished through the <span class="key-term">emunah</span> <span class="bracket">[faithfulness]</span> that is in the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Did you conduct your business with faithfulness?&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that is, that one should be faithful in one&rsquo;s speech, not to change one&rsquo;s word, etc.; see there.</p>

<h3>&sect;2</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And behold, all the acquisitions are in order to uphold the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>, so that one will no longer change <span class="bracket">[one&rsquo;s word]</span>. And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">hagbahah</span> <span class="bracket">[lifting]</span>, which is an especially important acquisition, for <span class="key-term">hagbahah</span> is that one literally lifts up the thing and carries it and raises it to return it to its place, in the aspect of <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> as mentioned above. For the <span class="key-term">hagbahah</span> is from the ground, where the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> fell, for they literally fell from heaven to earth. And the essence of <span class="key-term">hagbahah</span> is with the hands, which are the aspect of <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, as Rabbainu, may his light shine, wrote there, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And his hands were emunah&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Exodus 17:12]</span>. And through the <span class="key-term">hagbahah</span>, when one lifts it with one&rsquo;s hands from the ground, one raises and elevates the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> from their fallen state, as mentioned above, through the <span class="key-term">emunah</span> that is in the hands, as mentioned above. And then the transaction is upheld, since the <span class="key-term">emunah</span> has already been rectified and elevated, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;For I lift My hand to heaven&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Deuteronomy 32:40]</span>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Lift up your hands in holiness&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 134:2]</span> &mdash; that is, one raises the <span class="key-term">emunah</span> together with the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> to holiness, and then it is impossible to change the transaction any further &mdash; that is, to damage the faithfulness of one&rsquo;s word and change it &mdash; for the <span class="key-term">emunah</span> has already ascended together with the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> in the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> and has been rectified. And through this the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> is upheld, for this is the essence of the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;3</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">kinyan sudar</span> <span class="bracket">[acquisition by cloth/kerchief]</span>, which is a very important acquisition and is effective in every situation. For all <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> is exchange (<span class="key-term">chalifin</span>) &mdash; that is, one gives another person this thing and receives in return another thing or money. That is, one exchanges the holy <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> that have fallen, which exist in every object and need to be elevated. And when the time comes that the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> belonging to one&rsquo;s portions of <span class="key-term">nefesh, ruach, neshamah</span> <span class="bracket">[soul-levels]</span> have been exhausted and depleted, and one can no longer elevate the remaining <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span>, then one must sell it to another person who has portions of <span class="key-term">nefesh, ruach, neshamah</span> that correspond to those remaining <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span>. And one receives from one&rsquo;s fellow another object corresponding to one&rsquo;s own soul-portions, as is brought in the discourse <span class="verse">&ldquo;Vayehi Mikaitz&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan I:54]</span>.</p>

<p>And all the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> are sparks of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> <span class="bracket">[Sovereignty/the Shechinah]</span>, as is known. And garments are the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, as is brought in the words of Rabbainu, may his light shine <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan I:29]</span>. It turns out that the roots of all the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> are there <span class="bracket">[in the garments]</span>. And therefore the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> <span class="bracket">[husks/forces of impurity]</span> cling to the hems of the garments, as is known &mdash; this being the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> on the corners of the garments, in order to drive them away. As our Sages, of blessed memory, said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The garments of the scholars wear out from their rubbing&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Berachos 47b]</span> &mdash; for that is where they <span class="bracket">[the <span class="key-term">klipos</span>]</span> cling, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;to grasp the corners of the earth, and the wicked are shaken from it&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Job 38:13]</span> &mdash; the &ldquo;corners&rdquo; are the aspect of the four corners of the <span class="key-term">tallis</span>, from which the wicked &mdash; the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> &mdash; are shaken off and removed, for they had previously been clinging there, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">kinyan sudar</span> &mdash; that one acquires from the other by taking the corner of one&rsquo;s fellow&rsquo;s garment in one&rsquo;s hand, through which one elevates the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> from the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> clinging to the corner of the garment, as mentioned above. For each person must lift and elevate <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> that were until now with one&rsquo;s fellow &mdash; this being the essence of <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>, which is the aspect of exchange, as mentioned above. And this is accomplished by taking the corner of one&rsquo;s fellow&rsquo;s garment, where the roots of all the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> are, and one receives them and acquires them and elevates them from the <span class="key-term">klipos</span>. And this is <span class="key-term">kinyan sudar</span>. And through this the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> is upheld, for this is the essence of the upholding and rectification of the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> &mdash; to elevate the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> &mdash; and this is accomplished specifically through the garments, as mentioned above. And therefore the custom is to acquire by <span class="bracket">[taking]</span> the corner of the garment, as mentioned above. And all of this is done through the hands, for <span class="key-term">kinyan sudar</span> is with the hands, for the elevation of the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> is through the hands, which are the aspect of <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;4</h3>

<p class="no-indent">Also, the matter of <span class="key-term">kinyan sudar</span> can be understood according to the discourse <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hai man d&rsquo;azail l&rsquo;minsav&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan I:29]</span>; see there well. And this has already been explained somewhat above in Hilchos Shutafin b&rsquo;Karka <span class="bracket">[Laws of Land Partnerships]</span>. For the rectification of the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> and the rectification of the garments are one and the same aspect, and their rectification is through the whiteness (<span class="key-term">lavnunis</span>) that is drawn from the brain, through which the garments are rectified in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;white garments&rdquo;</span>; see there well. And this is also the rectification of speech, and this is also the rectification of <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>; see there.</p>

<p>And therefore all <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> is done through the garments, for they are one and the same aspect, as mentioned above. And when one receives a <span class="key-term">kinyan</span> <span class="bracket">[formal acquisition]</span>, one draws the rectification of the garments into the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>, and then the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> is properly rectified in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;white garments,&rdquo;</span> and through this it is upheld. For the blemish of the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> is the aspect of the blemish of the blood of the 365 sinews, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;For my iniquities have gone over my head; as a heavy burden, they are too heavy for me&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 38:5]</span>, as is explained there. And this is the blemish of the garments through a stain, which is also the blemish of blood in the aspect of menstrual blood, as is explained there.</p>

<p>And this itself is the blemish of one who changes one&rsquo;s word and lies in one&rsquo;s speech, for falsehood comes through the muddying of the blood, as Rabbainu, may his light shine, explained in the discourse <span class="verse">&ldquo;Rabbi Akiva said: When you reach the stones of pure marble&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan I:51]</span>. And this is also the aspect of speech that is not heard, which is not speech at all, as stated at the beginning of the discourse mentioned above &mdash; and this is because there is no good in it, as explained there, which is also the aspect of falsehood, meaning one who changes one&rsquo;s word as if one never spoke at all. And this is also the aspect of speech that is not heard, for <span class="verse">&ldquo;falsehood does not stand,&rdquo;</span> and no one listens to one&rsquo;s speech at all, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Such is the punishment of liars &mdash; even when they speak truth, no one listens to them&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Sanhedrin 89b]</span>. How much more so when one is entirely falsehood &mdash; one&rsquo;s speech is not heard and is not speech at all. And this is because there is no good in it, for falsehood is the evil and the impurity, as Rabbainu, may his light shine, explained.</p>

<p>And therefore, through the <span class="key-term">kinyan</span> one draws the aspect of the rectification of the garments, which is the rectification of the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>, the rectification of speech &mdash; which is the aspect of truthful speech. And then it is impossible to change any further, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;5</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of what is said <span class="bracket">[by the court]</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;He Who punished the generation of the Flood and the generation of the Dispersion &mdash; He will punish one who does not stand by one&rsquo;s word.&rdquo;</span> <span class="verse">&ldquo;The generation of the Flood and the generation of the Dispersion&rdquo;</span> specifically. And this is said when the acquisition was only through money. For the blemish of the generation of the Flood was the blemish of the Covenant, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For all flesh had corrupted its way upon the earth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 6:12]</span>. And this is the blemish of speech &mdash; one who does not stand by one&rsquo;s word &mdash; as is written in the discourse mentioned above, that the rectification of speech is through the aspect of the totality of the sinews, which is the aspect of the rectification of the Covenant, as is explained there in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;As an eagle stirs up its nest&rdquo;</span> etc.; see there.</p>

<p>And the primary blemish is when one arouses the intellect and draws the whiteness (<span class="key-term">lavnunis</span>) to other places, God forbid, which is an exceedingly great blemish, may the Merciful One save us. And this was the blemish of the generation of the Flood, who drew the whiteness of the brain to other places, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For all flesh had corrupted its way upon the earth&rdquo;</span> &mdash; they corrupted their way and spilled seed in vain. It turns out that they were drawing the whiteness of the brain to other places, and therefore their sin was too great to bear.</p>

<p>And this is also the aspect of the blemish of the generation of the Dispersion, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Come, let us make bricks&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 11:3]</span> &mdash; for they wanted to draw the aspect of whiteness, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;white garments,&rdquo;</span> to the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span> <span class="bracket">[the Other Side]</span>. For this was the essence of their intention &mdash; to draw the holiness to the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span> in the aspect of blemishing the Covenant, as mentioned above. And it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And all the earth had one language and unified words&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 11:1]</span> &mdash; and Rashi explains: in the Holy Tongue. <span class="verse">&ldquo;And it was when they journeyed from the east, and they found a valley in the land of Shinar&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that is Bavel. And Bavel is the aspect of the Aramaic language (<span class="key-term">lashon Targum</span>), for there the Aramaic language is spoken. And they wanted to suckle and draw the aspect of the Holy Tongue into the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span> through the Aramaic language, as is brought in the discourse <span class="verse">&ldquo;A prayer of Chavakuk&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan I:19]</span>. And therefore their punishment was that the languages were confused, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For there Hashem confused the language of all the earth&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">[Genesis 11:9]</span>.</p>

<p>It turns out that the blemish of the generation of the Dispersion was exactly the blemish of the generation of the Flood &mdash; namely, the aspect of drawing the whiteness to the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span>, God forbid. For the Holy Speech is also through the whiteness of the brain, as mentioned above, for the rectification of speech and the rectification of the Covenant are one and the same, as mentioned above. And so it is taught that the generation of the Flood and the generation of the Dispersion are one and the same aspect. And therefore in Egypt, where the reincarnated souls of the above <span class="bracket">[generations]</span> were present, as is taught in the writings of the Arizal &mdash; therefore they were compelled to work with mortar and bricks, as is known. And therefore the main labor was to produce a quota of bricks, for Pharaoh also wanted to draw the whiteness to the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span>, to Egypt, God forbid. And therefore, when he saw the sprouting horn of salvation through Moshe, he decreed not to give them any straw, yet they must still produce bricks, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And you shall provide the quota of bricks&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Exodus 5:18]</span> &mdash; for he wanted to overpower them so that they would draw the aspect of bricks, the aspect of whiteness, from themselves without any assistance from Egypt, in order to draw the aspect of the bricks of Yisrael themselves to the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span>, God forbid. But none of this availed him, for on the contrary, through their labor there they rectified and elevated the whiteness to holiness.</p>

<h3>&sect;6</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And this is also the aspect of the blemish of one who changes one&rsquo;s word in the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> that was already acquired through money. For money is the aspect of the brain and the life-force of the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;In the shadow of wisdom, in the shadow of money&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Ecclesiastes 7:12]</span>. And therefore all things in the world are acquired through money, for money is the aspect of the brain and the life-force of all things, as is brought above. And it is the aspect of whiteness, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the brain is white like silver&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Zohar]</span>.</p>

<p>And when the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> is conducted through money, it turns out that the aspect of whiteness has already been drawn. And therefore, when one then changes one&rsquo;s word, it turns out that one annuls the giving of the money; it turns out that the whiteness was drawn in vain, to the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span>, God forbid &mdash; and this is exactly the blemish of the generation of the Flood and the generation of the Dispersion, as mentioned above. And therefore we say: <span class="verse">&ldquo;He Who punished the generation&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;the generation of the Flood and the generation of the Dispersion&rdquo;</span> specifically, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>However, despite all this, the transaction is still not fully upheld. For the essence of the upholding of all things &mdash; that is, that the thing should be established and the external forces should not be able to cling to it and annul it &mdash; is specifically when the matter is drawn and clothed in <span class="key-term">asiyah</span> <span class="bracket">[action]</span>, in an actual deed, in a complete act. This is the aspect of the performance of <span class="key-term">mitzvos</span>, which must be done in an actual act specifically. And conversely, the blemish of transgressions is greatest when one performs an actual act, God forbid.</p>

<p>And therefore, when the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> is only in speech alone, even though it is a great blemish when one changes one&rsquo;s word and one is called lacking in faithfulness &mdash; nevertheless, the transaction is not upheld through this, since there was only speech and no action was yet performed. And even if one gave money, nevertheless it is not called an action, since money is in the aspect of the brain, as mentioned above. But when an action has already been performed &mdash; such as <span class="key-term">hagbahah</span> or <span class="key-term">meshichah</span> <span class="bracket">[pulling/drawing]</span> etc. &mdash; then it is impossible to change any further, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">kinyan sudar</span>, which always acquires. For when the aspect of the rectification of the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> is drawn in the aspect of the rectification of the garments &mdash; which is the aspect of drawing the whiteness into actual garments and coverings &mdash; then it is upheld and will not be annulled, as mentioned above. For this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">asiyah</span> <span class="bracket">[action]</span>, as mentioned above. For the essence of the rectification of <span class="key-term">asiyah</span> is that one makes a body and a garment for the holy life-force, so that the external forces will not cling to it, for they cling most to that which is unclothed (<span class="key-term">artilayin</span>). And therefore Adam, before the sin, it says <span class="verse">&ldquo;And they were both naked&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">[Genesis 2:25]</span> &mdash; for then there was no dominion of the external forces and they could be naked. But afterward, they knew that they were naked and needed to sew fig leaves to cover and clothe themselves, so that <span class="bracket">[the external forces]</span> would not cling to them, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And therefore, when the rectification of the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> is drawn into garments, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">asiyah</span> &mdash; for <span class="key-term">asiyah</span> is the ultimate level of garments, as is known &mdash; then it is impossible to change any further, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">kinyan sudar</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<hr class="divider">

<!-- ==================== MEKACH UMIMKAR 2 ==================== -->

<h2>Mekach Umimkar 2</h2>

<div class="halachah-intro">
<strong>Halachic Heading:</strong> The transaction is not finalized through words alone, but only through an act of acquisition (<em>kinyan</em>) &mdash; that is, <em>meshichah</em> (pulling), <em>mesirah</em> (delivery), or <em>hagbahah</em> (lifting), etc. Most acquisitions are through <em>kinyan sudar</em>. All of this applies to movable property; but land is acquired through money, as the detailed laws are set out in the Shulchan Aruch.
</div>

<p class="no-indent"><em>Based on Likutay Moharan I, Torah 25.</em></p>

<h3>&sect;1</h3>

<p class="no-indent">Based on the discourse beginning <span class="verse">&ldquo;Since the Bais HaMikdash was destroyed&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan I:25]</span>; see there well. And the general principle that emerges from there: that every person must extract oneself from the imaginative faculty and ascend to the intellect, etc. And know that at every level there exist these illusions, and when a person is uprooted and transferred from level to level, the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> <span class="bracket">[husks]</span> at that level intensify and do not let one enter, and one must prevail to break and subdue them, etc.</p>

<p>And the main subjugation of these <span class="key-term">klipos</span> that intensify when one moves from level to level is through the greatness of the Creator, blessed be His Name. And the revelation of the Creator&rsquo;s greatness is through the supernal colors (<span class="key-term">gvanin ilayin</span>) that exist in silver and gold, for there the supernal colors are clothed. And they are revealed when one gives charity (<span class="key-term">tzedakah</span>) to a worthy poor person &mdash; through this, all one&rsquo;s money is rectified and the supernal colors in the money are revealed. And then the greatness of the Creator is revealed and the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> at that level are subdued, etc. For the essence of the colors only shine in the hand of a Jewish person; but among the nations they are concealed. And because of this, they desire Jewish money, etc.; see all of this there well.</p>

<h3>&sect;2</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of all the acquisitions &mdash; that the transaction is not finalized through words alone, but only through an acquisition. For it has already been explained many times that all matters of <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> and buying and selling are for the purpose of elevating the fallen holinesses. And when one elevates these <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> and fallen holinesses through the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>, it turns out that they ascend from level to level, and then the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> at that level intensify, for at every level these illusions and <span class="key-term">klipos</span> exist, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And therefore the transaction is not finalized through words alone, for the main intensification <span class="bracket">[of the <span class="key-term">klipos</span>]</span> is at the time when they ascend from level to level, as mentioned above. And at the moment the transaction is finalized &mdash; when the object leaves one domain for another &mdash; that is the aspect of the refinement. And then the holiness that is there is refined and ascends from level to level, and then they <span class="bracket">[the <span class="key-term">klipos</span>]</span> intensify, as mentioned above. It turns out that at the time the object leaves one domain for another &mdash; which is the aspect of refinement and ascent from level to level &mdash; that is when they intensify, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And therefore, as long as the purchased object has not yet entered the buyer&rsquo;s domain, the transaction is not finalized through words alone. For even though <span class="bracket">[the seller]</span> has consented to sell to one&rsquo;s fellow, the transaction can still be reversed and annulled through their intensification &mdash; for they always intensify when <span class="bracket">[the sparks]</span> want to ascend from level to level. And therefore one must perform some act of acquisition.</p>

<p>And the essential acquisition, from the Torah itself, is through money, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And he shall give the money, and it shall be established for him&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Leviticus 27:19]</span>. For the essential acquisition is through money specifically, for there the supernal colors are revealed, which are the aspect of the greatness of the Creator, as mentioned above, through which the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> at that level are subdued, and one can ascend from level to level, and then the transaction is finalized &mdash; for the transaction is the aspect of the refinement and ascent from level to level, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;And he shall give the money, and it shall be established for him&rdquo;</span> &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;established&rdquo;</span> specifically, in the language of rising and ascent, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And the field of Efron was established&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">[Genesis 23:17]</span> &mdash; and our Sages, of blessed memory, expounded: &ldquo;It had a rising&rdquo; etc. For through money specifically, which is the aspect of the supernal colors as mentioned above, through this the transaction is finalized &mdash; which is the aspect of refinement, the aspect of rising and ascent from level to level, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;3</h3>

<p class="no-indent">However, our Sages, of blessed memory, enacted that money does not acquire <span class="bracket">[movable property]</span>. For in truth, even though money at its root is very exalted and contains the supernal colors, as mentioned above &mdash; nevertheless, below <span class="bracket">[in this world]</span>, the colors in silver and gold are not revealed except through rectifying the money &mdash; that is, through giving charity to a worthy poor person, etc., as mentioned above. For it is known that all things were damaged through the sin of Adam. And therefore the colors in silver and gold cannot be revealed except through rectification &mdash; that is, through charity, as mentioned above &mdash; but without the rectification, the colors are not revealed even in the hand of a Jewish person.</p>

<p>And therefore our Sages, of blessed memory, enacted that money does not acquire, for we do not have the power to subdue the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> at that level through money, since the colors in money are not always revealed, as mentioned above. And when the colors are not revealed, the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> at that level are not subdued, and therefore the transaction is not finalized, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And one may hint at this in the words of our Sages, of blessed memory, who said: From the Torah itself, money acquires; so why did the Sages say that pulling (<span class="key-term">meshichah</span>) acquires? As a precaution, lest <span class="bracket">[the seller]</span> say to him: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Your wheat was burned in the upper story (<span class="key-term">aliyah</span>).&rdquo;</span> And at first glance this is puzzling &mdash; why did our Sages, of blessed memory, seize upon &ldquo;upper story&rdquo; (<span class="key-term">aliyah</span>) specifically? They should have simply said: &ldquo;Your wheat was burned in my domain,&rdquo; or &ldquo;in the house and courtyard&rdquo; &mdash; why did they seize upon <span class="key-term">aliyah</span> specifically?</p>

<p>But one may hint at what was said above: that because we do not have the power to always reveal the supernal colors in money, as mentioned above, therefore the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> can still intensify at the time the transaction ascends (<span class="key-term">oleh</span>) from level to level, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;lest he say to him: your wheat was burned in the upper story (<span class="key-term">aliyah</span>)&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that is, at the time the transaction ascends from level to level, it is damaged and burned through the intensification mentioned above, which intensifies at the time of ascent &mdash; ascending from level to level &mdash; from which come all forms of damage.</p>

<h3>&sect;4</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore the transaction is finalized only through <span class="key-term">meshichah</span> <span class="bracket">[pulling]</span> or <span class="key-term">hagbahah</span> <span class="bracket">[lifting]</span> and the like. For the main thing is that the object must be in the buyer&rsquo;s domain for some time, so that it leaves one domain for another. And as soon as it enters the other&rsquo;s domain even once, the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> at that level have already been subdued. For their main intensification is at the time it leaves from level to level &mdash; that is, at the time it leaves from one domain to another, which is when the refinement is completed.</p>

<p>And therefore, as soon as one pulls the object or the like and it enters one&rsquo;s domain even briefly, the object has already ascended from level to level, since it has already left one domain for another. And through this the transaction is finalized, for the essence of finalizing the transaction is through this, as mentioned above. And therefore, even if immediately after the pulling etc. one returned and placed the object with the seller, the transaction is already finalized, since it already left one domain for another and the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> at that level were subdued, since it already entered one&rsquo;s domain, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;5</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore, with <span class="key-term">hekdesh</span> <span class="bracket">[consecrated property]</span>, money acquires even rabbinically. For <span class="key-term">hekdesh</span> money is holy, and the supernal colors are revealed in it since it is holy and the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span> has no hold on it; therefore the supernal colors are certainly revealed in <span class="key-term">hekdesh</span> money, and therefore with <span class="key-term">hekdesh</span>, money acquires, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And therefore also when a Jew buys from a non-Jew, money acquires according to many opinions. For Jewish money in relation to a non-Jew is very holy, and the supernal colors are revealed in it. As is well understood there in the words of Rabbainu mentioned above &mdash; that because of this, they desire Jewish money as if they had never seen money before, because in Jewish money the supernal colors are revealed; see there well. For in truth, even though Jewish money also requires rectification so that the colors will shine in it, as mentioned above &mdash; nevertheless, compared to the non-Jew, Jewish money is certainly very holy in the aspect of the shining of the colors, like the advantage of light over darkness <span class="source">[Ecclesiastes 2:13]</span>. As is understood in many places &mdash; that even the light that does not have the power to illuminate during the day, such as a candle, nevertheless at night and in the darkness it illuminates greatly, in the aspect of the advantage of light over darkness. And therefore certainly, Jewish money compared to the non-Jew illuminates greatly in the aspect of the colors mentioned above. And therefore, a Jew <span class="bracket">[buying]</span> from a non-Jew acquires through money according to many opinions, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;6</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of why <strong>land is acquired through money</strong>. For the main concealment of the colors in money &mdash; that the colors only shine through the rectification of charity, as mentioned above &mdash; all of this is because of the sin of Adam, through which <span class="bracket">[the lights]</span> were, as it were, darkened, and the lights of the colors were concealed and cannot be revealed except through rectification. For the essential lights of the colors in silver and gold are drawn only from Gan Eden, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;And a river went out from Eden to water the garden, and from there it divided into four headwaters. The name of the first is Pishon; it surrounds the entire land of Chavilah, where there is gold. And the gold of that land is good; there is the bedolach and the shoham stone&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 2:10&ndash;12]</span> &mdash; meaning the gold of holiness, drawn from the river that goes out from Eden, etc. &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the gold of that land is good&rdquo;</span> &mdash; &ldquo;good&rdquo; specifically, for there the lights of the colors are revealed, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;there is the bedolach and the shoham stone,&rdquo;</span> which are the aspect of supernal colors that are revealed in the good gold drawn from Gan Eden. For there, in Gan Eden, is the essential gold of holiness; for gold is counted among the thirteen canopies that the Holy One, blessed be He, made for Adam in Gan Eden, as is brought in Yechezkel <span class="source">[Ezekiel 28:13]</span>, and it is included among all the precious stones enumerated there: <span class="verse">&ldquo;odem, pitdah, and barekes, every precious stone&rdquo;</span> etc. That is the aspect mentioned above &mdash; that there the gold is comprised of many colors, which are the aspect of all the precious stones &mdash; for they are the totality of the colors, since each of the precious stones has its own distinct color, for they are the aspect of the supernal colors.</p>

<p>It turns out that the aspect of the gold of holiness, in which the lights of the colors are revealed, is the aspect of the good gold drawn from Gan Eden, as mentioned above. For there in Gan Eden all the supernal lights are revealed &mdash; which are the aspect of the supernal colors, as is known. And when Adam sinned and was expelled from Gan Eden, all the lights were concealed &mdash; that is, the lights of the supernal colors &mdash; for the silver and gold were blemished in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;in sorrow shall you eat&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 3:17]</span> &mdash; meaning diminished livelihood with great toil, which is drawn from the concealment of the supernal colors in silver and gold. For when the colors shine within silver and gold, great livelihood and abundance flow from them. And the main diminishment of livelihood, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;in sorrow shall you eat,&rdquo;</span> is because of the concealment of the colors.</p>

<p>It turns out that the primary concealment of the lights of the colors in silver and gold is because of the sin of Adam, as mentioned above. And the primary damage of Adam&rsquo;s sin &mdash; the contamination of the serpent &mdash; clings most to the earth, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Cursed is the ground on your account&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">[Genesis 3:17]</span>. And the essential rectification of Adam&rsquo;s sin depends on rectifying the earth &mdash; to remove the ground from its curse. For the earth is the root of all things in the world, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Everything was from the dust&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Ecclesiastes 3:20]</span>.</p>

<p>And this is what our Sages, of blessed memory, said <span class="source">[Yevamos 63a]</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Anyone who does not have land is not <span class="bracket">[considered]</span> a person (<span class="key-term">adam</span>).&rdquo;</span> For the essential aspect of being called <span class="key-term">adam</span> is when one rectifies the sin of Adam &mdash; for through Adam&rsquo;s sin, the aspect of <span class="key-term">adam</span> was blemished, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Man (<span class="key-term">adam</span>) in glory does not abide; he is likened to the beasts that perish&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 49:13]</span> &mdash; for through this, the power of the imaginative faculty &mdash; the animalistic power &mdash; was strengthened. And all of this was because the supernal colors that had been shining in the face were concealed &mdash; which are the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Divine image&rdquo;</span> (<span class="key-term">tzelem Elokim</span>) &mdash; for the colors are the aspect of the intellect, which is the <span class="key-term">tzelem Elokim</span>, the essential nature of the <span class="key-term">adam</span>. But when the colors are concealed, the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzelem Elokim</span> departs, and one is not called by the name <span class="key-term">adam</span>.</p>

<p>And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;<span class="key-term">Adam</span> in glory (<span class="key-term">yekar</span>) does not abide&rdquo;</span> &mdash; &ldquo;<span class="key-term">yekar</span>&rdquo; refers to the <span class="key-term">tefillin</span>, which are called <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;er</span> <span class="bracket">[glory/beauty]</span>, which is the aspect of the supernal colors &mdash; which are the aspect of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;er</span>, as is explained elsewhere. And through this, <span class="verse">&ldquo;he is likened to the beasts that perish,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And each person, to the extent that one merits to rectify the sin of Adam, through this one is called by the name <span class="key-term">adam</span>. And the essential rectification of Adam&rsquo;s sin &mdash; the contamination of the serpent &mdash; is through rectifying the land, as mentioned above. And therefore one who does not have land is not <span class="bracket">[called]</span> <span class="key-term">adam</span>, for everything that a person possesses, one refines it from the contamination of the serpent, and the main thing is to refine and rectify the land, which is the root of everything &mdash; and there is the essential rectification, as mentioned above. And when one rectifies the land, everything is rectified and everything is purified from the contamination of the serpent &mdash; from the sin of Adam &mdash; and then one is called by the name <span class="key-term">adam</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And when the land, which is the root of everything, is rectified, then everything is rectified. And therefore, when one acquires land &mdash; and it is a general principle that through all acquisitions one rectifies and refines the thing, as mentioned above &mdash; it turns out that when one acquires land and rectifies the aspect of land, which is the root of everything &mdash; which is the aspect of the general rectification of Adam&rsquo;s sin, to remove the ground from its curse, from the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Cursed is the ground&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; therefore, at the time of acquiring land, the lights of the colors in silver and gold are revealed, since it is the aspect of the general rectification of Adam&rsquo;s sin.</p>

<p>And therefore land is acquired through money. For at the time of purchasing land, the colors in the money are revealed, since it is the aspect of the general rectification of Adam&rsquo;s sin, as mentioned above. For the <span class="key-term">prutah</span> <span class="bracket">[coin]</span> of silver that one gives at the time of acquiring land is literally the aspect of a <span class="key-term">prutah</span> of <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span>, through which one rectifies all the money and the colors are revealed, as mentioned above &mdash; by giving a <span class="key-term">prutah</span> to a poor person and removing the poor person from the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;in sorrow shall you eat&rdquo;</span> through the money one gives &mdash; and through this the colors are revealed, for the main concealment was through the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;in sorrow shall you eat,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above. And therefore the <span class="key-term">prutah</span> of acquiring land is also in this aspect, for through this one rectifies and purifies the land from the contamination of the serpent, which is the root of everything, and through this everything is rectified and the colors are revealed &mdash; for the one depends on the other, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Cursed is the ground &mdash; in sorrow shall you eat&rdquo;</span> etc. And conversely, when one rectifies the ground, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;in sorrow&rdquo;</span> is rectified and the colors are revealed. And therefore land is acquired through money, for at the time of purchasing land, the colors are revealed, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is also the aspect of <span class="key-term">kinyan sudar</span> &mdash; the aspect of what is explained there in the discourse mentioned above regarding the colors mentioned above that are revealed in silver and gold &mdash; that they are the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;garments of salvation&rdquo;</span> etc.; see there well. And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">kinyan sudar</span>, that one acquires through garments, which are the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;garments of salvation,&rdquo;</span> the aspect of the supernal colors. For Rabbi Yochanan called his garments <span class="verse">&ldquo;my honorers&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Bava Kama 91b]</span> &mdash; the aspect of garments of honor and glory, the aspect of the totality of the colors. And through this one acquires everything, for the essential acquisition is through the revelation of the colors, through which the obstacles at each level are subdued and the thing is acquired and ascends from level to level, as mentioned above. For the colors in silver and gold are not always revealed, as mentioned above, and therefore one must acquire through garments &mdash; which are the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;garments of salvation,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above &mdash; for the colors are clothed in the garments, which are the aspect of the rectification of Adam&rsquo;s sin, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;And Hashem God made for Adam and his wife garments of skin and clothed them&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 3:21]</span>. For at first they were naked and then they could receive the lights of the colors without a garment; but afterward, through the sin, <span class="bracket">[the lights]</span> were concealed and can only be revealed through the aspect of garments, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;And He made &hellip; and clothed them.&rdquo;</span></p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span>, through which the colors are revealed, as mentioned above &mdash; for <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> is the aspect of garments, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;I clothed myself in righteousness (<span class="key-term">tzedek</span>)&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Job 29:14]</span>, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;garments of salvation,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above &mdash; which are the aspect of the colors, as is explained well in the discourse mentioned above: that when the lights of the colors are revealed and shine, they are in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;garments of salvation, a cloak of righteousness (<span class="key-term">tzedakah</span>)&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Isaiah 61:10]</span>; see there well.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">kinyan sudar</span>, that one acquires through garments &mdash; which acquires in every matter. And most acquisitions are through this, for the garments are the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;garments of salvation,&rdquo;</span> the aspect of the revelation of the supernal colors, which are the aspect of the greatness of the Creator, blessed be He &mdash; through which one acquires and rectifies and elevates all things in the world, as mentioned above.</p>

<p style="text-align:center; color:var(--accent); font-style:italic;">Blessed be Hashem forever, Amen and Amen.</p>

<hr class="divider">

<!-- ==================== MEKACH UMIMKAR 3 ==================== -->

<h2>Mekach Umimkar 3</h2>

<div class="halachah-intro">
<strong>Halachic Heading:</strong> The matter of <em>kinyan sudar</em> and all the other acquisitions, which are <em>mesirah</em> (delivery), <em>meshichah</em> (pulling), and <em>hagbahah</em> (lifting).
</div>

<p class="no-indent"><em>Based on Likutay Moharan I, Torah 159.</em></p>

<h3>&sect;1</h3>

<p class="no-indent">Based on the Torah that begins <span class="verse">&ldquo;Know that there is an intermediary&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan I:159]</span>; see there, the entire Torah. And the general principle: there are two types of Torah study. There is the study of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, which ascends to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, who is the intermediary between Him, blessed be He, and the world. And then from the right and left aspects of the Torah &mdash; which are fire and water &mdash; there is produced spiritual abundance and material abundance. That is, from the right aspect comes spiritual abundance &mdash; the supernal flow for all the heavenly beings, the angels and <span class="key-term">seraphim</span>, etc. And from the left aspect comes material abundance for the lower worlds, etc.</p>

<p>However, not every person merits that one&rsquo;s study ascends to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, etc. And then, when one&rsquo;s study does not ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, when one studies, vapors go out from one&rsquo;s mouth, etc. And the nature of the Torah is to raise itself upward to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, as mentioned above, but it cannot ascend because this student does not merit that one&rsquo;s study should ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, as mentioned above. And behold, one&rsquo;s Torah rises up, trying to ascend upward, but it cannot, as mentioned above. And meanwhile night falls, and then all the <span class="key-term">gardinai nimusin</span> <span class="bracket">[angelic prosecutors]</span> come out, etc., and they strike against it, etc. And then this Torah is scattered in the air, and all people in the world draw from this Torah that was scattered in the air.</p>

<p>And according to the nature of the person to whom this Torah arrives, so is what is made from it. For a kosher person, etc., or a great person and <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, when they receive from these Torahs that were scattered &mdash; it becomes the dew of Torah for them, etc., according to the nature of the receiver. For some, Torah insights (<span class="key-term">chiddushei Torah</span>) are produced from these Torahs, etc. And this is the aspect of the right that is in the Torah. But from the aspect of the left, the opposite is produced &mdash; namely, the 39 categories of work (<span class="key-term">lamed-tes melachos</span>) &mdash; for these Torahs that reach people who are not worthy, the opposite is produced for them from the dew mentioned above. That is, the aspect of the 39 categories of work, which is the opposite of the dew (ta&ldquo;l = 39) of Torah &mdash; meaning, a new arousal toward the toil of commerce and the pursuit of livelihood, which is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;By the sweat of your brow shall you eat bread&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">[Genesis 3:19]</span>. And this is the aspect of right and left in the Torah: for in Torah study that ascends to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, from the right and left are produced spiritual and material abundance, etc.; and from this study that cannot ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, from the right and left are produced the dew of Torah or the 39 categories of work, etc., as mentioned above; see all of this there well.</p>

<h3>&sect;2</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>. For the essence of <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> is in order to refine the holy sparks that are clothed in all the objects of commerce, as is known. And the essence of the refinement is to refine the holy sparks &mdash; which are the aspect of sparks of the letters of the holy Torah &mdash; from the aspect of the 39 categories of work, which are the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;By the sweat of your brow shall you eat bread,&rdquo;</span> from which all the activities and toil of commerce and all the types of crafts and all the businesses in the world are drawn &mdash; all of which are included in the 39 categories of work, as is known. For the root of the 39 categories of work in holiness is the aspect of the letters of the holy Torah, the aspect of the holy sparks. And one must refine all these letters and holy sparks from within the aspect of the 39 categories of work &mdash; which are all the activities of <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;3</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And the essence of the refinement &mdash; the reason we must toil and labor to refine them &mdash; is drawn from those Torahs that do not merit ascending to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, which are scattered in the air. From these, sometimes the 39 categories of work are produced, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;By the sweat of your brow,&rdquo;</span> etc., as mentioned above. And therefore one must toil in <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> and in crafts, and strive and beseech Hashem, blessed be He, that one should merit to perform all the 39 categories of work and all the activities of <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> with great holiness &mdash; so that one may merit to refine from there all the sparks of the letters of the Torah, mentioned above, that fell there, from which these 39 categories of work were produced, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;4</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And it is impossible to refine these holy sparks from within the 39 categories of work except when one connects oneself to the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> of the generation, who is the aspect of Yosef. For Yosef is the ruler, he is the one who provides grain, etc. <span class="source">[Genesis 42:6]</span> &mdash; all the sales and acquisitions in the world are all accomplished through the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> of the generation, who is the aspect of Yosef, as mentioned above. As it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And all the earth came to Egypt, to Yosef, to buy&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 41:57]</span> &mdash; for all the earth, meaning all the world who are engaged in <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>, in truth all business is to refine refinements, to refine holy sparks from the depths of the <span class="key-term">klipos</span>. And all of them are in the aspect of those who descend to Egypt, for all the exiles are referred to by the name &ldquo;Egypt&rdquo;; see there &mdash; for they constrict (<span class="key-term">meitzrim</span>) Yisrael <span class="source">[Bereishis Rabbah 16]</span>.</p>

<p>And the main exile is the exile of the soul &mdash; that the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span>, the nations, do not allow the Jewish soul to return to Hashem and truly cleave to Him. And therefore, one who enters the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span>, where the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> and the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span> cling and surround the holy sparks within the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> &mdash; one who enters there is in the aspect of descending to the Egyptian exile, which includes all exiles &mdash; which is the aspect of the exile of the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span> upon the Jewish soul and the holy sparks attached to it. And then, when the Jewish soul descends into the exile mentioned above &mdash; that is, when one engages in <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> &mdash; one cannot stand there and succeed in accomplishing one&rsquo;s task completely, to refine the sparks from there and emerge from there in peace, except by connecting oneself then to the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> of the generation, who is the aspect of Yosef, through whom all the refinements in the world are accomplished.</p>

<p>This is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;And all the earth came to Egypt, to Yosef, to buy&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that all the merchants in the world engaged in <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> are all compelled to come to the Egyptian exile where all the sparks are captive in exile, as mentioned above. Therefore they are all compelled to come there in order to elevate the sparks from there. And when they come there to the Egyptian exile, they need to come to Yosef &mdash; the aspect of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> &mdash; to buy and to trade and to make all the acquisitions through him specifically, for through the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> all the refinements in the world are accomplished, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;5</h3>

<p class="no-indent">For in truth, all the life-force of the entire world and its fullness is only from the holy Torah, as is known, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;In the beginning, God created the heavens and the earth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 1:1]</span> &mdash; &ldquo;in the beginning&rdquo; refers to the Torah, which is called <span class="verse">&ldquo;the beginning of wisdom&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 111:10]</span>. And with it Hashem created the entire world and its fullness, and it is the life-force of all things and all objects in the world. It turns out that in every object in the world, the letters of the holy Torah are clothed, for it is its life-force.</p>

<p>And if we all merited to be as we should, in accordance with His good will in truth, and to study Torah for its own sake (<span class="key-term">lishmah</span>) in truth &mdash; then all things would be refined, even all the mundane objects, for they all receive their life-force from the Torah, as mentioned above. But since not every person merits that one&rsquo;s study ascends to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, as mentioned above, and when one&rsquo;s study does not ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, the Torah is scattered, etc., and sometimes the 39 categories of work are produced from it, etc., as mentioned above &mdash; therefore one must toil in <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> and strive greatly that the <span class="key-term">masa umattan</span> should be conducted with great holiness, so that perhaps one will merit to refine the sparks &mdash; the letters of the Torah clothed in the 39 categories of work, which were produced from the letters of the Torah whose study was not adequate, which was scattered in the air, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And therefore the main refinement and rectification is through the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> of the generation, who is the aspect of Yosef, as mentioned above. For the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> studies Torah for its own sake, and one&rsquo;s study ascends to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, and through one all the abundances in the world are drawn &mdash; spiritual abundance and material abundance, etc., as mentioned above. And even when the Torahs of the rest of the world &mdash; who do not merit that their study should ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, and their study is scattered in the air, as mentioned above &mdash; reach the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, they become the dew of Torah, the opposite of the 39 categories of work. It turns out that the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> also refines these studies of the rest of the world from the aspect of the 39 categories of work, for with the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> they become the dew of Torah &mdash; namely, Torah insights, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;6</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore, every person, at the time of one&rsquo;s study and service, must connect oneself to the true <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span> of the generation. For certainly not every person merits that one&rsquo;s study and service ascends to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>. And then, when one&rsquo;s study and service does not ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, it is scattered in the air and could reach an unworthy person, and from one&rsquo;s Torah the aspect of a poison of death could be produced, God forbid &mdash; which is the 39 categories of work, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;By the sweat of your brow shall you eat bread,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore, every person must intend during one&rsquo;s study and service to connect oneself to the true <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span> of the generation. And then one will merit that even though one&rsquo;s study does not ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, at least one&rsquo;s study will be scattered and arrive at the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, who will produce the dew of Torah from it. And then, when the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> produces the dew of Torah &mdash; that is, Torah insights &mdash; from one&rsquo;s study, and the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> studies and reveals this Torah that one merited to derive from those Torahs that were scattered in the air, as mentioned above &mdash; then it returns and becomes spiritual abundance and material abundance for all beings above and below, as mentioned above. For now it has become the Torah of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, from whose Torah comes spiritual and material abundance, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>It turns out that through the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, all the studies of the rest of the world &mdash; who do not merit that their study should ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, as mentioned above &mdash; are also refined, for with the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> they become the dew of Torah, the opposite of the 39 categories of work, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;7</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Happy is the person who has not walked in the counsel of the wicked &hellip; but in the Torah of Hashem is his desire, and in His Torah he meditates day and night&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 1:1&ndash;2]</span>. For King David, peace be upon him, opened his book with the praise of those who truly serve Hashem, and he found no quality better for a person than distancing oneself from the counsel of the wicked and drawing near to the <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span>. For this is the foundation and the essential principle upon which everything depends &mdash; for the main refinement and rectification of every person in the world is through the true <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span>.</p>

<p>And therefore the main thing is to distance oneself from the counsel of the wicked, etc., who oppose and contend against the true <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span>. For certainly not every person merits that one&rsquo;s study and service ascends to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, as mentioned above. For even important and worthy people in truth, and even complete <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span> &mdash; very few merit that their study ascends to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, for this is only achieved by an exceedingly great <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>. And therefore, one who is not at such a level of righteousness &mdash; if one does not intend to connect one&rsquo;s study and service to the true <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span>, then, God forbid, one&rsquo;s Torah will be scattered and will reach unworthy people, and from one&rsquo;s Torah will be produced the 39 categories of work, etc. &mdash; where the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> and <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span> cling, as mentioned above. Therefore one must intend to connect oneself to the <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span> of the generation, and then one will merit that one&rsquo;s Torah will ascend in the aspect of the right, and from one&rsquo;s Torah will be produced the dew of Torah, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Happy is the person who has not walked in the counsel of the wicked &hellip; but in the Torah of Hashem is his desire, and in His Torah he meditates day and night.&rdquo;</span> That is, it is good for a person who distances oneself from the wicked, etc. &mdash; rather, the essence of all one&rsquo;s Torah and service is included in <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Torah of Hashem&rdquo;</span> &mdash; which is the Torah of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span>, for all one&rsquo;s desire and will is toward them, and one connects to them during the time of one&rsquo;s Torah study and service. And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;but in the Torah of Hashem is his desire, and in His Torah he meditates&rdquo;</span> etc. That is, <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Torah of Hashem&rdquo;</span> refers to the Torah of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, whose every study ascends immediately to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, who is included in Him, blessed be He. And therefore one&rsquo;s Torah and study is literally <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Torah of Hashem.&rdquo;</span> But the study of the rest of the world that does not ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span> is called <span class="verse">&ldquo;his Torah&rdquo;</span> &mdash; for it does not ascend and become included in Him, blessed be He, immediately, and therefore it is called &ldquo;his Torah&rdquo; and not &ldquo;the Torah of Hashem.&rdquo; But the main rectification for this is to connect oneself with all one&rsquo;s desire and will to the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> whose study is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Torah of Hashem,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above &mdash; and then one&rsquo;s Torah will also be rectified, for it will reach the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> and become the dew of Torah. And then the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> will innovate Torah insights through it, and then it will return and become included and ascend to its root, for now it has become the Torah of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, which is literally <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Torah of Hashem,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;but in the Torah of Hashem is his desire, and in His Torah he meditates day and night&rdquo;</span> &mdash; even though one studies &ldquo;his Torah&rdquo; and does not merit that one&rsquo;s study should ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span> and be called literally <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Torah of Hashem&rdquo;</span> &mdash; nevertheless, <span class="verse">&ldquo;in the Torah of Hashem is his desire,&rdquo;</span> for all one&rsquo;s salvation and aspiration and desire is in <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Torah of Hashem,&rdquo;</span> which is the Torah of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> to whom one connects oneself and in whom one is included, as mentioned above. Through this, one&rsquo;s Torah also returns and is included in <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Torah of Hashem,&rdquo;</span> for from one&rsquo;s Torah the dew of Torah is produced by the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And he shall be like a tree planted by streams of water&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">[Psalms 1:3]</span>. <span class="verse">&ldquo;A tree planted by streams of water&rdquo;</span> &mdash; this is the aspect of the Torah of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> that ascends to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>. For the Torah is called a tree, the aspect of the Tree of Life, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;It is a tree of life to those who grasp it&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">[Proverbs 3:18]</span>. And the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span> is called <span class="verse">&ldquo;streams of water,&rdquo;</span> the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the stream of God is full of water&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 65:10]</span>. For the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span> is the aspect of the sea, into which all the rivers flow, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;all the rivers flow to the sea&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">[Ecclesiastes 1:7]</span>, as is known. That is, this person who merits to connect oneself to the <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span> of the generation &mdash; one&rsquo;s Torah is considered like a tree planted by streams of water, like the study of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> that ascends to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span> &mdash; which is called a tree planted by streams of water, as mentioned above &mdash; from which is produced spiritual abundance for the upper worlds and material abundance, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;whose fruit it gives in its season&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 1:3]</span> &mdash; this is the aspect of spiritual abundance, which is the primary fruit. For the primary reward of the Torah is for the world that is entirely long <span class="bracket">[the World to Come]</span>, as is known &mdash; which is the aspect of spiritual abundance. And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;whose fruit it gives in its season&rdquo;</span> &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;in its season&rdquo;</span> specifically, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;At this time it shall be said to Yaakov and to Yisrael: What has God wrought?&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Numbers 23:23]</span> &mdash; which alludes to the fact that the <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span> enliven all the angels and all the upper worlds, as our Sages, of blessed memory, learned <span class="source">[Yerushalmi Shabbos ch. 2]</span> from this verse: that in the future, the <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span> will have a place within the angels, and the angels will ask Yisrael: <span class="verse">&ldquo;What has God wrought?&rdquo;</span> As Rabbainu, of blessed memory, cited this teaching elsewhere; see there.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of spiritual abundance &mdash; for the main abundance of the angels and the upper worlds that the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> provides them is revealing to them the knowledge of His Godliness, blessed be He &mdash; for this is their primary life-force and sustenance &mdash; that the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> gives them spiritual abundance through one&rsquo;s Torah that ascends to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, as mentioned above. That is, one reveals to them through one&rsquo;s Torah the knowledge of Godliness, which is their primary life-force, as mentioned above. And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;whose fruit it gives in its season&rdquo;</span> &mdash; this is the aspect of spiritual abundance, as mentioned above. <span class="verse">&ldquo;And its leaf does not wither, and all that he does prospers&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 1:3]</span> &mdash; this is the aspect of material abundance that descends to this world from the left aspect of the Torah, which is the aspect of leaves &mdash; the aspect of the mundane conversation of a Torah scholar, which is the aspect of the left compared to the body of the Torah. And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;and all that he does prospers&rdquo;</span> &mdash; the aspect of material action, meaning material abundance &mdash; livelihood and wealth &mdash; for in all of them the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, who is the aspect of Yosef, prospers, as mentioned above, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and all that he does, Hashem causes to prosper in his hand&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 39:3]</span>, as mentioned above. For one draws all the abundances &mdash; spiritual and material abundance, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And King David, peace be upon him, said that this person who connects oneself to the true <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span> and does not walk in the counsel of the wicked, etc., who distance from them, as mentioned above &mdash; rather, all one&rsquo;s desire and will is to be included in them and in their Torah, which is called <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Torah of Hashem,&rdquo;</span> etc., as mentioned above &mdash; then this person is like a tree planted by streams of water, etc. That is, one&rsquo;s study is actually considered like the Torah of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, which is called a tree planted, etc. &mdash; &ldquo;whose fruit,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; for one also merits to be included in him through the connection to him. Through this, one&rsquo;s Torah comes to the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> and becomes the dew of Torah &mdash; namely, the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>&rsquo;s Torah insights. It turns out that one&rsquo;s Torah returns and becomes the Torah of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, which is <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Torah of Hashem&rdquo;</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of a tree planted, etc. &mdash; for from it flows spiritual and material abundance, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And <span class="bracket">[David]</span> concluded: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Not so the wicked &mdash; but they are like chaff that the wind drives away&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 1:4]</span>. For their Torah is scattered in the air literally like chaff that the wind drives away, for the cold wind &mdash; the aspect of all the <span class="key-term">gardinai nimusin</span> mentioned above &mdash; strikes against it, and from it is produced the 39 categories of work, which are the opposite of the dew (ta&ldquo;l) of Torah, as mentioned above. And the 39 categories of work are the aspect of chaff and straw, which are the refuse &mdash; the aspect of the husk that precedes the fruit &mdash; which is why all the toil of all the 39 categories of work exists: to refine the wheat &mdash; the 22 letters of the Torah &mdash; from the chaff and straw, which are the refuse, the aspect of the 39 curses, as is known &mdash; which are the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;By the sweat of your brow shall you eat bread,&rdquo;</span> etc. That is, for the wicked who are not connected to the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, from their Torah that is scattered in the air is produced the 39 categories of work, which is the aspect of chaff that the wind drives away, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;8</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And this is <span class="source">[Genesis 44:18]</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And Yehudah approached him and said: Please, my lord, let your servant speak a word in the ears of my lord, and let not your anger burn against your servant, for you are like Pharaoh.&rdquo;</span></p>

<p>Yehudah &mdash; this is the aspect of the collective of Yisrael, who are all called <span class="key-term">Yehudim</span> <span class="bracket">[Jews]</span> after Yehudah. Yosef is the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> of the generation, as mentioned above. And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;And Yehudah approached him&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that Yisrael beseech the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, the aspect of Yosef, that all the Torah they will study &mdash; even though they do not merit that their Torah should ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span> &mdash; at least their Torah should ascend and reach the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, and then it will be considered as if their Torah ascended to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span> itself.</p>

<p>And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;Let your servant speak a word in the ears of my lord.&rdquo;</span> And Rashi explains: &ldquo;Let my words enter your ears.&rdquo; That Yehudah &mdash; the aspect of the collective of Yisrael &mdash; beseeches that the words of their Torah should enter the ears of the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, so that from their Torah should be produced the dew of Torah and not the opposite, God forbid &mdash; which is the 39 categories of work, which are the aspect of the left, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;By the sweat of your brow shall you eat bread&rdquo;</span> &mdash; which are the aspect of burning anger, the severity of judgment, the aspect of the 39 curses, as mentioned above. And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;let not your anger (<span class="key-term">apecha</span>) burn against your servant&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that from the Torah should not be produced, God forbid, the aspect of burning anger, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the sweat of your brow (<span class="key-term">apecha</span>),&rdquo;</span> etc., the aspect of the 39 categories of work, as mentioned above. Rather, may we merit that our study should ascend to the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, and then the dew of Torah &mdash; Torah insights &mdash; will be produced from it, and then the study will return and ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span> and become included in Him, blessed be He. For now it has become the Torah of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, which is literally <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Torah of Hashem,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;for you are like Pharaoh&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that Yehudah &mdash; Yisrael &mdash; gives the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> the honor of the <span class="key-term">malchus</span> <span class="bracket">[sovereignty]</span>, as is explained there. That is, they accept the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> as king over them, in order that all their Torah and service should be included in him and ascend through him to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;9</h3>

<p class="no-indent">For the essential cause of all the sparks falling into the place of the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> was through the aspect of <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> <span class="bracket">[dispute/conflict]</span> drawn from self-aggrandizement &mdash; the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;I shall reign&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Zohar]</span> &mdash; from which came the essential <span class="key-term">shevirah</span> <span class="bracket">[shattering]</span> and the falling of the sparks, as is known. For the <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> came because each spark wanted to be the greatest, wanting the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;I shall reign.&rdquo;</span></p>

<p>And afterwards as well, the essential falling of the sparks &mdash; namely, that the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> continue to draw sustenance from holiness &mdash; is all through <span class="key-term">machlokes</span>. For the main sustenance of the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> is from <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> &mdash; which is the opposite of peace, the opposite of the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, which is called <span class="verse">&ldquo;peace,&rdquo;</span> as is known. For there &mdash; at the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, which is the aspect of peace &mdash; is where all the study and service must ascend, as mentioned above. And the <span class="key-term">machlokes</span>, which is drawn from <span class="verse">&ldquo;I shall reign&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that is, there is one who wants to aggrandize himself and make himself great, claiming that he is the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> of the generation &mdash; this is the very opposite of the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, which is the aspect of peace, the aspect of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, which is the aspect of Yosef who is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, as mentioned above &mdash; for to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, to the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, everything must ascend, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And when one grasps a different <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> &mdash; that is, one who is not truly worthy of being the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> of the generation, the aspect of Yosef mentioned above, but only claims so &mdash; then one&rsquo;s study, since it does not ascend to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span> through the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, is scattered in the air, and the 39 categories of work are produced from it, etc., as mentioned above. And since these 39 categories of work were produced from this <span class="key-term">machlokes</span>, it turns out that the sparks that fell into the 39 categories of work &mdash; their falling was all because of the <span class="key-term">machlokes</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;10</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And this itself is the concept of the halachos of buying and selling and all the modes of acquisition. For through commerce one performs refinements from the <span class="key-term">haichlei hatmuros</span> <span class="bracket">[chambers of exchange]</span>. This is the entire matter of commerce &mdash; it exists solely because sparks fell into the <span class="key-term">haichlei hatmuros</span>, through which the abundances and objects became exchanged. In all of them there are holy sparks, and items belonging to one person&rsquo;s soul-portion of <span class="key-term">nefesh, ruach, neshamah</span> are in another person&rsquo;s hands, and the other&rsquo;s are in one&rsquo;s hands, and so on &mdash; innumerable exchanges and substitutions. Because of this, one must engage in commerce. The essential commerce is exchange &mdash; this person has this item and that person has another item, and they exchange and buy from one another. Through this, the sparks are re-exchanged and the sparks leave the <span class="key-term">haichlei hatmuros</span>, as the item passes from this one to that one and from that one to this one, until each spark returns to its place and root &mdash; which is its essential rectification and refinement.</p>

<p>For as long as the sparks are not in their place, but one person&rsquo;s are in another&rsquo;s hands, as mentioned above, the <span class="key-term">chitzonim</span> <span class="bracket">[external forces]</span> have a hold on them, since the primary hold of the <span class="key-term">chitzonim</span> is from the aspect of the <span class="key-term">haichlei hatmuros</span>, as mentioned above. But when they are re-exchanged and return to their owners and their root, that is their rectification. This is the aspect of the refinement accomplished through all commerce, as is brought. For all commerce is exchange, as mentioned above, through which the sparks are re-exchanged and the sparks leave the <span class="key-term">haichlei hatmuros</span> &mdash; since the item returned from this one to that one and from that one to this one, until it returned to the person it properly belongs to, according to the sparks within that item that specifically belong to that person&rsquo;s soul, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;11</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And the essential refinement is through the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> of the generation, the aspect of Yosef. For the essential refinement of commerce is to refine commerce from the 39 categories of work, as mentioned above. And therefore, through the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> of the generation, all the commerce in the world is rectified, for one refines and elevates the holy sparks from within the 39 categories of work through which all the activities of commerce came into being, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And therefore all modes of acquisition are derived from the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> of the generation, the aspect of Yosef, who is the main one through whom all the refinements of commerce are accomplished, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;12</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And conversely, one who is distant from the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> &mdash; all the more so when one disputes him, God forbid &mdash; then <span class="verse">&ldquo;in the way a person wants to go, one is led.&rdquo;</span> Then one&rsquo;s study, when scattered in the air, reaches unworthy people and is transformed into the 39 categories of work, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;13</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of the blemish of the <span class="key-term">Shevatim</span> <span class="bracket">[Tribes]</span> who disputed Yosef until they sold him for silver. For Yosef was then the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> of the generation, and they all needed to receive from him, and all their service and study needed to come to him and ascend through him. Even though they were all very great <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span>, the essential one was Yosef the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> &mdash; the aspect of the point of truth among the <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span> &mdash; to whom Yaakov transmitted everything, as Rashi explains on the verse: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And Yisrael loved Yosef more than all his sons, for he was the son of his old age&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 37:3]</span>.</p>

<p>The true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, who is the aspect of Yosef, has compassion on the generation &mdash; the aspect of the totality of the Tribes &mdash; and constantly tells them his dreams and his words, so that they should merit to connect themselves to him. He alerts them that they all need to connect themselves to him, for the entire ascent of their Torah and service is through him. This is the aspect of the dream he told them: that he saw <span class="verse">&ldquo;we were binding sheaves in the field, and behold, your sheaves surrounded and bowed to my sheaf&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 37:7]</span>. That is, he saw that they were all engaged in their service, performing unifications and binding connections &mdash; level to level and world to world &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;binding sheaves&rdquo;</span> &mdash; which are bonds and bundles, the aspect of holy unifications and connections made in the upper worlds through the service of the true <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span>. <span class="verse">&ldquo;And behold, your sheaves surrounded and bowed to my sheaf&rdquo;</span> &mdash; all their service needed to come to the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> and be encompassed within him, for the essential purpose of all the connections and unifications is to elevate everything to the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span>, which is accomplished only through the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, the aspect of Yosef, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>But they did not want to believe in this and said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Shall you indeed reign over us? Shall you indeed rule over us? And they hated him even more on account of his dreams and his words&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 37:8]</span>. For they say that whatever the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> reveals &mdash; his Torah, his innovations, and his perceptions &mdash; to the Children of Yisrael, his intention is, God forbid, for self-aggrandizement, to reign and rule over them. They dispute him and pursue him with every kind of persecution &mdash; just as the brothers of Yosef wanted to kill him and cast him into a pit. Even those who somewhat sided with him and had mercy on him proposed to sell him for twenty pieces of silver. That is, they sell the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> and conceal him from the world for the sake of money &mdash; for the craving of wealth. For when one blemishes the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, one&rsquo;s study no longer ascends to the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, and then the 39 categories of work are produced from one&rsquo;s study, as mentioned above &mdash; the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;By the sweat of your brow shall you eat bread&rdquo;</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of the craving for wealth. It turns out that through blemishing the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, one falls into the craving for wealth, as is explained elsewhere in the Torah <span class="verse">&ldquo;Tzavisa tzedek&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan I:23]</span>. This is the aspect of selling Yosef for silver &mdash; for one falls into the craving for wealth by blemishing the honor of the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>This is the aspect of all the modes of acquisition, and the primary one is <span class="key-term">kinyan sudar</span>. For through commerce one performs refinements from the <span class="key-term">haichlei hatmuros</span> <span class="bracket">[chambers of exchange]</span>. This is the entire matter of commerce &mdash; it exists solely because sparks fell into the <span class="key-term">haichlei hatmuros</span>, through which the abundances and objects became exchanged. In all of them there are holy sparks, and items belonging to one person&rsquo;s soul-portion are in another person&rsquo;s hands, and the other&rsquo;s are in one&rsquo;s hands &mdash; innumerable exchanges and substitutions. Because of this, one must engage in commerce. The essential commerce is exchange, as mentioned above, through which the sparks leave the <span class="key-term">haichlei hatmuros</span> and return to their root &mdash; which is their essential rectification and refinement. And the essential refinement is through the <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> of the generation, the aspect of Yosef. For the essential refinement of commerce is to refine commerce from the 39 categories of work, which are drawn from the Torahs of those who dispute the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span>, which are scattered in the air and transformed into the 39 categories of work, as mentioned above.</p>

<p class="section-note">The text is incomplete here &mdash; <em>chaseir</em>.</p>

<p style="text-align:center; color:var(--accent); font-style:italic;">Blessed be Hashem forever, Amen and Amen.</p>

<hr class="divider">

<!-- ==================== MEKACH UMIMKAR 4 ==================== -->

<h2>Mekach Umimkar 4</h2>

<div class="halachah-intro">
<strong>Halachic Heading:</strong> The transaction is not finalized except through an act of acquisition (<em>kinyan</em>), etc.
</div>

<p class="no-indent"><em>Based on Likutay Moharan I, Torah 266.</em></p>

<h3>&sect;1</h3>

<p class="no-indent">Based on the Torah beginning <span class="verse">&ldquo;And for his cattle he made <em>sukkos</em>&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan I:266]</span>; see there. And the general principle: that through blemishing the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, one falls from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> <span class="bracket">[influx/abundance]</span> of <em>adam</em> <span class="bracket">[man]</span> &mdash; which is from the place of <span class="key-term">binah</span> <span class="bracket">[understanding]</span>, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;<em>Ima</em> <span class="bracket">[the Mother]</span> who shelters over her children,&rdquo;</span> the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;if you call to <em>binah</em>&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Proverbs 2:3]</span> &mdash; and then one falls to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> <span class="bracket">[animal]</span> and draws the vitality and sustenance of the animals. Through this, one causes the animals to die before their time, since one has taken their sustenance, etc.; see there. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and for his cattle he made <em>sukkos</em>,&rdquo;</span> for the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> is for the sake of one&rsquo;s cattle, as mentioned above. Also, those who engage in building &mdash; it harms them if they do not build the house with wisdom, etc. But through the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, which is the aspect of intellect and knowledge, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;if you call to <em>binah</em>,&rdquo;</span> through this one can build a house, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Through wisdom a house is built&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Proverbs 24:3]</span>, etc. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;And Yaakov traveled to Sukkos and built himself a house&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 33:17]</span>, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of Shavuos, etc., for the Torah emerges from the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, etc. And therefore immediately after Sukkos comes Simchas Torah, etc. &mdash; for through entering the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> they themselves become the aspect of Torah, etc. And then the Torah begins, which is <span class="verse">&ldquo;Bereishis&rdquo;</span> <span class="bracket">[&ldquo;In the beginning&rdquo;]</span> &mdash; the aspect of <em>bayis</em> <span class="bracket">[house]</span>, that is, the letter <em>beis</em> of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Bereishis,&rdquo;</span> etc.; see there.</p>

<h3>&sect;2</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of the rectification of the sin of Adam HaRishon. For it is known that during these holy days &mdash; the days of Tishrei &mdash; we must rectify the sin of Adam HaRishon, who ate from the Tree of Knowledge on the day he was created, which is Rosh HaShanah. And we must, every year, in every generation, rectify this sin. We are engaged in this rectification from Rosh HaShanah until Shemini Atzeres, as is explained in the writings of the Arizal.</p>

<p>For Adam HaRishon, through eating from the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil, fell from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>. For the defining characteristic of man is <span class="key-term">daas</span> <span class="bracket">[knowledge/awareness]</span>, and he blemished the <span class="key-term">daas</span> by eating from the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil and was drawn after the animalistic desires, which are the aspect of the evil within the Tree of Knowledge. Through this he fell from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And you shall eat the grass of the field&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 3:18]</span> &mdash; which is animal food, as our Sages said: that Adam HaRishon said, <span class="verse">&ldquo;Shall I and my donkey eat from the same trough?&rdquo;</span> Only that Hashem, blessed be He, had compassion on him even then, and immediately told him: <span class="verse">&ldquo;By the sweat of your brow you shall eat bread&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 3:19]</span>. As our Sages said <span class="source">[Avos d&rsquo;Rabbi Nassan, ch. 1]</span>: When the Holy One, blessed be He, told Adam HaRishon, <span class="verse">&ldquo;And you shall eat the grass of the field,&rdquo;</span> he trembled and said, <span class="verse">&ldquo;Shall I and my donkey eat from the same trough?!&rdquo;</span> Once he heard <span class="verse">&ldquo;By the sweat of your brow you shall eat bread,&rdquo;</span> his mind was settled.</p>

<p>That is, through his sin he caused himself to fall to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, as mentioned above &mdash; this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall eat the grass of the field,&rdquo;</span> the aspect of &ldquo;I and my donkey at the same trough.&rdquo; Only that Hashem, blessed be He, even while cursing him, had compassion on him and hinted to him that it is within his power to rectify the blemish, and immediately told him: <span class="verse">&ldquo;By the sweat of your brow you shall eat bread.&rdquo;</span> That is: it is possible for you to return and draw the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, which is the aspect of <em>lechem</em> <span class="bracket">[bread]</span>. But it will come to you through great toil and exertion, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;by the sweat of your brow you shall eat bread.&rdquo;</span> For because of the sin, one must toil and exert oneself greatly until one refines the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from the aspect of <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>.</p>

<p>This is the aspect of how all the grain falls into chaff and straw, which are the aspect of the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> <span class="bracket">[husks]</span> that cover the fruit &mdash; which are the aspect of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, for chaff and straw are animal food, as are bran and coarse bran. And within them precisely the wheat is clothed &mdash; the wheat being human food. A person needs great toil and exertion before refining the wheat &mdash; which is human food, the aspect of <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> &mdash; from the aspect of <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, which is the chaff, straw, bran, and coarse bran. And all of this is because Adam HaRishon blemished and fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>. According to his sin, he deserved to draw sustenance only from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>; only through Hashem&rsquo;s mercy was it placed in his power to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>. This is the aspect of the power a person has to refine food from chaff, straw, and all the other husks and waste that cover it &mdash; all of which are drawn from the blemish that one fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>. But this requires great exertion, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;by the sweat of your brow you shall eat bread,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above. And just as it is in the physical realm, so it is in the spiritual: one must do <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span> and many rectifications, each person according to the blemishes one has caused by being drawn after the sin of Adam HaRishon, engaging in <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span> and rectification before refining one&rsquo;s sustenance from the aspect of <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>. And we are engaged in this rectification especially from Rosh HaShanah until the end of Sukkos, which is Shemini Atzeres, for then we are engaged in rectifying the sin of Adam HaRishon (as is brought in the writings of the Arizal) who blemished in this way, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And through the great rectification that all Yisrael accomplish during the Ten Days of <span class="key-term">Teshuvah</span>, from Rosh HaShanah until Yom HaKippurim, until their sins &mdash; which are the aspect of the sin of Adam HaRishon &mdash; are forgiven, through this Hashem, blessed be He, shows His great love toward us and brings us into the holy and awesome <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;<em>Ima</em> who shelters over her children,&rdquo;</span> the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;if you call to <em>binah</em>,&rdquo;</span> which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, as explained in the Torah mentioned above. That is, through this He shows us that our sins have already been forgiven and we have already rectified the blemish of Adam HaRishon, who through his sin fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> &mdash; for now we are sitting in the holy <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, from which the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> is drawn &mdash; the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <span class="key-term">binah</span> and <span class="key-term">daas</span> &mdash; to know and recognize our Creator and Fashioner, blessed be His Name, through this sustenance. This is the essential <span class="key-term">daas</span> that is drawn through the holy <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, and this is the essential defining characteristic of man. Therefore the primary mitzvah of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> is eating, drinking, and sleeping, and one recites the blessing only at the time of eating. For the essential aspect of the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> is to draw the vitality and <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, which is drawn through eating in the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> &mdash; which is the vitality of the human being.</p>

<h3>&sect;3</h3>

<p class="no-indent">For this reason, all the early <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span>, who are the patriarchs of the world, were shepherds of animals. For they were engaged in rectifying the sin of Adam HaRishon, as is known. Therefore they were shepherds of animals, in order to restore the pasture and <span class="key-term">shefa</span> to the animals &mdash; to rectify what Adam HaRishon had blemished by falling to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> and drawing the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> to himself, thereby causing the death of animals before their time. And now they rectify this by shepherding animals and restoring the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of the animals to the animals. And so it is understood from the words of Rabbainu, of blessed memory, elsewhere <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan II:63]</span>, that the essential intention in shepherding animals was to refine the spirit of man from the spirit of animal, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Who knows the spirit of man&hellip;&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Ecclesiastes 3:21]</span>; see there. That is, to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> &mdash; for they purified themselves of all animalistic desires and restored the sustenance of the animals to its proper place. Through this they drew for themselves only the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, pure and clean, without the waste that is the aspect of chaff and straw, as is known; understand this. Therefore the great <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span> are called &ldquo;shepherds,&rdquo; in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">shivah ro&rsquo;im</span> <span class="bracket">[Seven Shepherds]</span> &mdash; because they restored the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> and pasture of the animals to the animals, and took nothing for themselves from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, for they purified themselves completely from animalistic desires and merited the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;4</h3>

<p class="no-indent">Therefore all the Seven Shepherds enter the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, for the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> &mdash; this being the rectification drawn through the Seven Shepherds, as mentioned above. And the essential completion of the rectification of all the Seven Shepherds is through Dovid HaMelech, peace be upon him, who is the seventh &mdash; for he completed and will complete the rectification in fullness, through Mashiach Tzidkainu, who is Dovid himself. Therefore the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> is called by his name &mdash; the aspect of <span class="key-term">Sukkas Dovid</span> <span class="bracket">[the Booth of David]</span>. For Dovid is the King of Yisrael, and the essential <span class="key-term">shefa</span> is drawn through the king, as is explained in the words of Rabbainu, of blessed memory. Therefore the king of Yisrael must be especially careful not to fall, God forbid, to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, for upon him depends the sustenance of all Yisrael. Therefore he must engage in this especially &mdash; to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em>.</p>

<p>And this is what is written regarding Dovid: <span class="verse">&ldquo;From behind the nursing ewes He brought him, to shepherd Yaakov His people&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 78:71]</span>. That is, precisely through having been a shepherd of animals he merited to become the shepherd of Yisrael &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;to shepherd Yaakov His people.&rdquo;</span> As our Sages said: he was diligent and watchful over the animals, as is brought in Rashi&rsquo;s commentary &mdash; that he would send out the young kids first and feed them the tender tips of the grass, etc., then the older goats, and then the aged ones, etc. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: &ldquo;This one is fit to shepherd My people!&rdquo;</p>

<p>At first glance, it is puzzling that through shepherding animals one should merit kingship. And regarding Dovid himself, it is puzzling why he engaged in this &mdash; did he not have <span class="key-term">mitzvos</span> and acts of kindness of greater importance to engage in? He could have engaged in supporting the poor and the like, which is certainly a greater mitzvah &mdash; to have compassion on them &mdash; than to engage in shepherding animals and having compassion on them! But in truth, his essential intention in this was in order to rectify the sin of Adam HaRishon, for he needed to engage in this especially, as is known. Therefore he was compelled to engage in shepherding animals and to have compassion on them and to watch over them well &mdash; in order to restore and rectify what Adam HaRishon had blemished. That is, to restore the sustenance of the animals to its place, and to restore to each individual animal its proper sustenance, so that the animals would receive their sustenance and vitality as is fitting for each one, so that he could return to his elevated status and draw and receive the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above. Therefore it was precisely through this that he merited kingship &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;to shepherd Yaakov His people&rdquo;</span> &mdash; for the king must draw the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> to all his people. Therefore it is impossible for him to be king unless he merits to draw the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> and is clean and pure from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> &mdash; which he merited through shepherding animals, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;5</h3>

<p class="no-indent">And in this you will see wonders: for this reason Nevuchadnetzar the wicked, who is the opposite of Dovid HaMelech, peace be upon him &mdash; for this one built the <span class="key-term">Beis HaMikdash</span> <span class="bracket">[Holy Temple]</span> and settled Yisrael upon their land, while that one destroyed it and exiled them from their land &mdash; therefore Hashem, blessed be He, punished him with a strange and terrifying punishment that has never been heard of: he was turned into an animal for seven years. For so it was fitting and appropriate for him, since he is the wicked kingdom that first overpowered Yisrael &mdash; who are the aspect of the kingdom of Dovid, whose sustenance is from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> &mdash; for Yisrael are called <em>adam</em>, etc. Therefore he became an actual animal, for because he blemished the holy kingdom, the kingdom of Dovid, so greatly &mdash; for he was the first to destroy the <span class="key-term">Beis HaMikdash</span>, which is the House of Dovid, etc. &mdash; which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above &mdash; because of this, through his wickedness, he stood against them so greatly; therefore he fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> so greatly until he became an actual animal for seven years.</p>

<p>And he was an animal for specifically seven years, corresponding to the Seven Shepherds whom he blemished. For they all engaged in drawing the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, which is the aspect of the kingdom of Yisrael, the kingdom of Dovid, as mentioned above. And he blemished this so greatly; therefore he fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> so greatly until he became an actual animal for seven years, as mentioned above. And the ways of Hashem are just, for He returned his deeds upon his head and showed him what he had blemished, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;6</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;On that day I will raise up the <em>Sukkas</em> Dovid that has fallen&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Amos 9:11]</span>, and adjacent to it: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Behold, days are coming when the plowman shall overtake the reaper&hellip; and the mountains shall drip sweet wine&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Amos 9:13]</span>. For <span class="key-term">Sukkas Dovid</span> is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, and then blessing and great abundance is drawn, and the grain and all the fruits are blessed, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the plowman shall overtake the reaper&hellip; and the mountains shall drip sweet wine.&rdquo;</span> For the essential obstruction of blessing is from the sin of Adam HaRishon, through which the earth was cursed on his account &mdash; which was caused by falling to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall eat the grass of the field,&rdquo;</span> etc., as mentioned above. Therefore, through raising the <span class="key-term">Sukkas Dovid</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of the rectification for this, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above &mdash; through this, great blessing and abundance will be drawn to all the grain and fruits.</p>

<p>Therefore, everywhere that it consoles Yisrael regarding the final redemption, it mentions each time the great abundance that will exist then: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The vine shall give its fruit,&rdquo;</span> etc. For the essential redemption &mdash; the aspect of the kingdom of Dovid, Mashiach &mdash; is through the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Sukkas Dovid</span>. That is, to restore and refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em>, through which the curse that Adam HaRishon caused is annulled, and great blessing is drawn to all the grain and fruits, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;In the future, the Land of Yisrael will produce baked loaves&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Shabbos 30b]</span> &mdash; for the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> will be drawn refined, without chaff, straw, or waste, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;7</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of why Sukkos is called <span class="key-term">Chag Ha&rsquo;Asif</span> <span class="bracket">[the Festival of Ingathering]</span>, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And the Festival of Ingathering you shall make for yourself, when you gather in your produce from the field&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Exodus 34:22]</span>. For all the days of summer the grain lies in the field, and the field is the place of animals and beasts. As long as the grain is in the field, it has not yet been refined from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, for it is still clothed in chaff, straw, bran, and coarse bran, etc. The essential refinement is when one gathers it from the field into the house, for in the house one refines it from all the waste until one makes from it bread for human consumption &mdash; the aspect of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>.</p>

<p>Therefore, at the time of the ingathering, the holy Torah commanded us to enter the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, in order to merit the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> that is drawn from the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>. For then is the time for this, because then is the time of ingathering, when one gathers the grain from the field into the house &mdash; which is the aspect of refinement from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>. Therefore one needs the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> then, for specifically through the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> one has the power to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;8</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of why the essential <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> is made from <span class="key-term">p&rsquo;soles goren v&rsquo;yekev</span> <span class="bracket">[the waste of the threshing floor and winepress]</span>, as our Sages said on the verse <span class="verse">&ldquo;when you gather in,&rdquo;</span> etc.: &ldquo;Scripture speaks of the waste of the threshing floor and winepress.&rdquo; For through this one rectifies what Adam HaRishon &mdash; or any person through his sins &mdash; corrupted by falling to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> through being drawn after animalistic desires. For now one lifts and elevates the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> &mdash; which is the aspect of the waste of the threshing floor and winepress &mdash; and makes from it specifically a <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>. Through this precisely, <span class="verse">&ldquo;<em>Ima</em> shelters over her children,&rdquo;</span> and one merits the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>. It turns out that with the very thing one corrupted, one is rectified &mdash; for so it must be in the rectification of everything: to rectify with the very thing one corrupted.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of all the <span class="key-term">korbanos</span> <span class="bracket">[sacrifices]</span> &mdash; that when a person sins, one brings an animal as a <span class="key-term">korban</span>. At first glance, this is puzzling. But according to the above, it is well explained: for through one&rsquo;s sin, having been drawn after animalistic desires, one fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> and thereby caused the death of animals before their time, since one took their sustenance. Therefore one must bring an animal as a <span class="key-term">korban</span>. And in slaughtering and putting to death the animal for the sake of a <span class="key-term">korban</span>, one rectifies what one blemished &mdash; having taken the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> and drained its vitality until it was fit to die before its time. For now one puts it to death through the slaughter for a <span class="key-term">korban</span> and elevates it as a pleasing fragrance to Hashem &mdash; which is a great rectification for the animal, for now one restores the vitality and <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of the animal to a level far greater than before, since it has ascended as a <span class="key-term">korban</span>. It turns out that through the <span class="key-term">korban</span> of an animal, one rectifies what one blemished regarding the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> and vitality of animals. Therefore the <span class="key-term">korbanos</span> atone for all sins, which are the aspect of the blemish of the sin of Adam HaRishon, who fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> and took their vitality, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p class="section-note"><span class="bracket">(For even though Rabbainu, of blessed memory, wrote the essential matter of this teaching regarding the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> &mdash; that through this one causes the death of animals, etc. &mdash; that is, the essential blemish depends on the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, as is explained there. But certainly through every sin and transgression one also causes this, for through every sin one blemishes the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, from which the Torah emerges &mdash; that is, one blemishes the <span class="key-term">daas</span>, for a person does not commit a sin unless a spirit of folly enters into him. And through this one falls to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, God forbid, etc., commensurate with the blemish. And there is more to say about this, and it will be explained elsewhere, God willing.)</span></p>

<h3>&sect;9</h3>

<p class="no-indent">Therefore, on Sukkos, more <span class="key-term">korbanos</span> are offered than at any other time of the entire year. For then one needs to elevate and rectify the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> and restore and draw the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above &mdash; which one merits through <span class="key-term">korbanos</span>, as mentioned above. Therefore, on Sukkos, seventy bulls are offered, corresponding to the seventy nations. For the nations of the world are called <em>behemos</em> <span class="bracket">[animals]</span>, and Yisrael are called <em>adam</em>. As our Sages said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You are called <em>adam</em>&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Yevamos 61a]</span>, etc.</p>

<p>The essential <span class="key-term">shefa</span> descends only for the sake of Yisrael, who are called <em>adam</em>. For everything was created and sustained and given abundance for the sake of the <em>adam</em> &mdash; which is Yisrael. And when the <em>adam</em> &mdash; the person of Yisrael &mdash; falls from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> and draws the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> and diminishes their sustenance, as mentioned above, then one draws from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of the nations, who are called <em>behemah</em>. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;So shall the children of Yisrael eat their bread impure among the nations&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Yechezkel 4:13]</span> &mdash; for when they are in exile among the nations, they eat their bread impure; that is, their sustenance is the aspect of impure bread, which is the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of the <em>behemos</em>, from which all the animalistic desires derive, as mentioned above. And from this is the essential prolongation of the exile. For when Yisrael fall from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> and draw from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, God forbid &mdash; which is the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of the nations &mdash; then the nations, the aspect of <em>behemos</em>, have no <span class="key-term">shefa</span> or vitality, to the point that it could cause their death before their time, as mentioned above. Then sometimes the <em>behemos</em>, the aspect of the nations, overpower and draw from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, the aspect of Yisrael. As it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And when Yisrael would sow, Midyan and Amalek would come&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Judges 6:3]</span>, etc. And from this comes the overpowering of wild animals and beasts to cause harm, God forbid, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And the teeth of beasts I will send against them&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Deuteronomy 32:24]</span>, etc.</p>

<p>For when the <em>adam</em> receives the essential <span class="key-term">shefa</span> &mdash; that is, the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> &mdash; and he draws the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> to the <em>behemos</em>, which are the aspect of the nations, then he rules over them. But conversely, when he falls to their sustenance, the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, God forbid, then they rule over him, God forbid. As it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And have dominion over the fish of the sea and over every living creature&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 1:28]</span>. And Rashi explains: if one merits &mdash; one rules over them; if one does not merit &mdash; one becomes subordinate before them. That is, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And in truth, when the <em>behemos</em>, the aspect of the nations, overpower and consume the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, which is Yisrael, it harms them greatly, and from this itself they are consumed and die &mdash; for the food of <em>adam</em> harms <em>behemah</em>, as is seen through the senses. And likewise, the food and <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of Yisrael harms the nations, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;a time when man rules over man to his detriment&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Ecclesiastes 8:9]</span>. Only temporarily do they have dominion over Yisrael, because they take the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, which is Yisrael, and rule over them &mdash; since Yisrael blemished and fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;And it shall be, when you are aggrieved, you shall break his yoke from upon your neck&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 27:40]</span>. This verse, <span class="verse">&ldquo;and it shall be, when you are aggrieved&rdquo;</span> <span class="bracket">[<em>v&rsquo;hayah ka&rsquo;asher tarid</em>]</span>, has no straightforward explanation, and Rashi himself struggles greatly with its interpretation; see there. But now it is explained according to its plain sense: <span class="verse">&ldquo;and it shall be, when you are aggrieved&rdquo;</span> <span class="bracket">[<em>tarid</em>]</span> &mdash; that is, when you descend from your <span class="key-term">shefa</span>. That is, when Yisrael fall to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, which is the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of Eisav, as mentioned above &mdash; and then the <em>behemah</em>, the aspect of Eisav, descends from its own <span class="key-term">shefa</span>, for it has no <span class="key-term">shefa</span> since the <em>adam</em>, the aspect of Yisrael, has taken its sustenance &mdash; then <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall break his yoke from upon your neck.&rdquo;</span> That is, you will cast off the yoke of the <em>adam</em> &mdash; Yisrael &mdash; who rules over you always, for you will overpower him and take his <span class="key-term">shefa</span>. For since the <em>adam</em>, Yisrael, changed the order and fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, and the <em>behemah</em> has no <span class="key-term">shefa</span>, the <em>behemah</em> is forced to descend to an even lower level of <span class="key-term">shefa</span> &mdash; according to the order of creation, in which the animal is lower than man and under man&rsquo;s dominion &mdash; and since man descended to its level of sustenance, it must descend further. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;when you are aggrieved&rdquo;</span> &mdash; <em>tarid</em> literally &mdash; that his sins cause you to descend from your sustenance, as mentioned above. Then <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall break his yoke from upon your neck&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that you will also change the order and take his sustenance and rule over him.</p>

<p>But this is only temporary, during the time of the overpowering of the exile &mdash; when they take the essential <span class="key-term">shefa</span> and Yisrael are sustained from the leftovers, as is stated in the holy Zohar. But it cannot remain this way, for it is impossible to change the order of creation permanently. For Yisrael will return to their dominion and take their sustenance &mdash; the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> &mdash; and the animals and nations who draw from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> will be greatly harmed by it, for the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> harms <em>behemah</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And even now, during the exile, each person of Yisrael, to the degree that one merits to fulfill the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> in completeness &mdash; so one merits even during the exile the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>. For the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> protects and shelters over one, and from there the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> is drawn, which is drawn from the place of <span class="key-term">binah</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore, on Sukkos, seventy bulls are offered corresponding to the seventy nations. For now, through the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, we restore to the seventy nations &mdash; who are the aspect of <em>behemos</em> &mdash; their sustenance. For now we return to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> through the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, as mentioned above, and then the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of the animals returns to the animals. And then the animals, which are the aspect of the nations, are sustained, for we restore to them their sustenance.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of what our Sages said: that the bulls diminish progressively, like the festival offerings of the Chag <span class="source">[Sukkah 55b]</span>. That is, their greatness and dominion diminishes through this. For all their dominion was because Yisrael fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, through which they overpowered and changed the order and drew from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above. But now Yisrael returns to their sustenance &mdash; the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> &mdash; and they return to their sustenance, that of <em>behemos</em>. And then the <em>adam</em>, the aspect of Yisrael, rules over the <em>behemos</em>, the aspect of the nations. But even so, it is to their benefit, for through this they are sustained. For when they drew from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> &mdash; even though they ruled through it &mdash; it was to their detriment, for the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> harms <em>behemah</em>, as mentioned above. But now, on Sukkos, when the <em>behemos</em> &mdash; the nations &mdash; return to their own sustenance, then they have endurance, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore the final redemption is called by the name <span class="key-term">Sukkas Dovid</span>, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;On that day I will raise up the <em>Sukkas</em> Dovid that has fallen,&rdquo;</span> etc. For the essential redemption &mdash; to annul the dominion of the nations and to restore Yisrael to their dominion &mdash; is through the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, for through this one merits the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> and vitality of <em>adam</em>, which is the aspect of Yisrael, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;10</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of why a transaction is not finalized through words alone, but through an act of acquisition. For all commerce and all business is for the purpose of refining the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> that fell through the sin of Adam HaRishon, as is known. For through his sin, when it was decreed upon him <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall eat the grass of the field; by the sweat of your brow you shall eat bread,&rdquo;</span> great exertion is needed before one draws the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> and sustenance. The essential exertion is before one refines the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> and sustenance from the aspect of <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>. This is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall eat the grass of the field; by the sweat of your brow you shall eat bread&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that you need great exertion, <span class="verse">&ldquo;by the sweat of your brow,&rdquo;</span> before you refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;grass of the field&rdquo;</span> &mdash; the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> &mdash; to the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;bread&rdquo;</span> &mdash; the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, as explained above.</p>

<p>This is the aspect of all commerce: they are all refinements that refine the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> from the sin of Adam HaRishon and elevate them from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>. For the distinction between <em>adam</em> and <em>behemah</em> is essentially the <span class="key-term">daas</span>. And whenever something is not in its proper place and is in exile, it is in the aspect of the absence of <span class="key-term">daas</span>, as is brought in the words of Rabbainu, of blessed memory, elsewhere <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan II:10]</span>, where he cites the teaching of our Sages: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Go to Ammon and Moav whose minds are settled,&rdquo;</span> as it says: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Moav has been at ease since his youth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Jeremiah 48:11]</span>. Therefore all the fallen <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span>, before they are refined and return to their place, are in the aspect of the absence of <span class="key-term">daas</span> &mdash; because they are in exile and not in their place. And then they are in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, which is the absence of <span class="key-term">daas</span>.</p>

<p>This is the aspect of all commerce and business: the goods and merchandise must pass and travel from one person to another, and from this one to that one, until they return to their proper place. Through this precisely, the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> and sustenance are drawn to the person. For each time the item passes from one domain to another, the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> are refined and ascend from their exile and draw closer to their place. Through this they are refined and ascend each time from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore a transaction is not finalized through words alone, but through an act of acquisition. And all acquisitions are performed with the hands &mdash; such as <span class="key-term">meshichah</span> <span class="bracket">[pulling]</span>, <span class="key-term">hagbahah</span> <span class="bracket">[lifting]</span>, etc. For it is impossible to elevate the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> to their place, to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, except through the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, as mentioned above &mdash; which is the aspect of <em>yadayim</em> <span class="bracket">[hands]</span>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and in the shadow of My hand I have sheltered you&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Isaiah 51:16]</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, as is known. For the hands are the vessels of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, which is in the place of <span class="key-term">binah</span> &mdash; the aspect of the heart, as mentioned above &mdash; for the hands are close to the heart, as is known through the senses. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Let us lift our hearts to our palms&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Lamentations 3:41]</span>, etc.</p>

<p>For it is impossible to draw the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> except through the hands, which are the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> &mdash; and not through speech alone. For <em>adam</em> was created by the Hand, and everything else was created through an utterance, as Rashi explains on the verse <span class="verse">&ldquo;And God created the man in His image&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 1:27]</span>: everything was created through an utterance, but he was created by the Hand, as it says: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And You placed Your palm upon me&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 139:5]</span>. That is, as mentioned above: for the <em>adam</em> must be nourished and sustained from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, which is drawn from the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> &mdash; the aspect of <span class="key-term">binah</span>, the heart &mdash; which is the aspect of hands, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;let us lift our hearts to our palms,&rdquo;</span> the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;You placed Your palm upon me,&rdquo;</span> which is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and I have sheltered with My palm upon you&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Exodus 33:22]</span> &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;v&rsquo;sakosi&rdquo;</span> being the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>. That is, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore the transaction &mdash; which is to refine from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> &mdash; is not finalized through words, for then it is still in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, since everything was created through an utterance. Rather, it is finalized through the hands &mdash; and then it is refined to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, who was created by the Hand, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> &mdash; the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;You placed Your palm upon me,&rdquo;</span> the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and I have sheltered with My palm,&rdquo;</span> etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;11</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of <span class="key-term">kinyan sudar</span> <span class="bracket">[acquisition through a garment]</span>, which effects acquisition in all matters. For garments are the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Ananai Kavod</span> <span class="bracket">[Clouds of Glory]</span> &mdash; which are the aspect of garments, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;when I made the cloud its garment&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Job 38:9]</span>, as is brought in his words, of blessed memory.</p>

<h3>&sect;12</h3>

<p class="no-indent">Therefore, one&rsquo;s courtyard and house effect acquisition for a person regarding all acquisitions, as our Sages said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;A person&rsquo;s courtyard acquires for him,&rdquo;</span> etc. For the essential building of a house is through the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;And Yaakov traveled to Sukkos and built&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 33:17]</span>, etc., as mentioned above. For this is the essential aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>: that it is at the time of <span class="key-term">asif</span> <span class="bracket">[ingathering]</span>, at the time when one gathers the grain &mdash; the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> &mdash; from the field into the house, which is the aspect of elevating and refining it from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em>, as explained above. Therefore a person&rsquo;s house and courtyard effect acquisition regarding all acquisitions in the world. For the essential purpose of all acquisitions is through refining the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em>, which is accomplished through the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, from which the essential building of the house derives, as mentioned above. Therefore all wealth and <span class="key-term">shefa</span> is named for the house, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The wealth of his house&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 49:17]</span>, etc. For the essential <span class="key-term">shefa</span> is when it enters the house, which derives from the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, from which the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> flows &mdash; the essential <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of holiness, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;13</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of <span class="key-term">matnos kehunah</span> <span class="bracket">[the priestly gifts]</span>: one must give from everything gifts to the <span class="key-term">kohein</span> <span class="bracket">[priest]</span>. For the <span class="key-term">kohanim</span> are sanctified with the holiness of their father Aharon, and from Aharon HaKohein derives the essential holiness of the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> &mdash; the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Ananai Kavod</span>, which existed in the merit of Aharon, as our Sages said. Therefore, whatever Hashem, blessed be He, bestows upon a person, one must give from it gifts to the <span class="key-term">kohein</span> &mdash; in order to rectify and refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> through this from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, which one merits through the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, <span class="key-term">Ananai Kavod</span>, which are the aspect of Aharon HaKohein, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the great mitzvah of <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> <span class="bracket">[charity]</span> &mdash; for through <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> one becomes of the status of <em>adam</em>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Let us make man&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 1:26]</span>; and it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And the name of the man&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Ruth 2:19]</span>, etc., as is brought in his words, of blessed memory, citing the Zohar; see there. That is, one must be careful to give <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> from everything that Hashem, blessed be He, bestows upon a person, in order to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from the sin of Adam HaRishon &mdash; from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em> &mdash; which one merits through <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span>, through which one becomes of the status of <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above. For the essential poverty is drawn from the sin of Adam HaRishon, through falling to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall eat the grass of the field; by the sweat of your brow,&rdquo;</span> etc. And through <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> one rectifies the poverty and refines the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore, on Sukkos one must increase greatly in <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> and <span class="key-term">chesed</span> <span class="bracket">[kindness]</span>, as is brought in the writings of the Arizal, that he would increase in <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> on the eve of Sukkos; see there. And in the holy Zohar, that one must invite guests into the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> corresponding to the <span class="key-term">ushpizin kadishin</span> <span class="bracket">[holy guests]</span>, etc. For on Sukkos one must draw the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> through the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, as mentioned above. And for this one needs <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span>, through which one becomes of the status of <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;14</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">maaser sheini</span> <span class="bracket">[the second tithe]</span>: one must separate from the grain and bring it up to Yerushalayim. For the essential aspect of the holiness of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, at its root, is in Yerushalayim &mdash; as we bless: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Who spreads the <em>sukkah</em> of peace over us and over all His people Yisrael and over Yerushalayim.&rdquo;</span> Therefore the <span class="key-term">Beis HaMikdash</span> is there, for it is the essential House of holiness of Yisrael, the aspect of the <em>beis</em> of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Bereishis,&rdquo;</span> from which the holiness of all the houses of Yisrael is drawn, as is understood from the Torah <span class="verse">&ldquo;Bereishis&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan II:67]</span>; see there. For the holiness of the <span class="key-term">Beis HaMikdash</span> is drawn from the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;And Yaakov traveled to Sukkos and built himself a house.&rdquo;</span> Therefore the <span class="key-term">Beis HaMikdash</span> is called <span class="key-term">Sukkas Shalem</span> <span class="bracket">[the Booth of Shalem, i.e. Jerusalem]</span>.</p>

<p>Therefore one must separate from the grain <span class="key-term">maaser sheini</span> and bring it up to Yerushalayim &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Sukkas Shalem</span> &mdash; in order to refine and elevate the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, which one merits through the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<hr class="divider">

<h2 style="font-size:1.15em; margin-top:1.5em;">Hilchos Onaah</h2>

<h3>&sect;15</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of the prohibition of <span class="key-term">onaah</span> <span class="bracket">[fraud/overcharging]</span>: it is forbidden to defraud one&rsquo;s fellow in money, and even in words. For <span class="key-term">onaah</span> is a blemish of the <span class="key-term">daas</span>, for one misleads the <span class="key-term">daas</span> of one&rsquo;s fellow. Therefore it is a great prohibition, beyond the prohibition of theft itself. For the essential purpose of all commerce is to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from the aspect of <em>behemah</em> &mdash; which is the absence of <span class="key-term">daas</span> &mdash; to the aspect of <em>adam</em> &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">daas</span>. And when one defrauds one&rsquo;s fellow in commerce and misleads him, one blemishes the <span class="key-term">daas</span>, as mentioned above, and is unable to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from the aspect of <em>behemah</em>. On the contrary &mdash; one falls even further to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> by blemishing the <span class="key-term">daas</span> through the <span class="key-term">onaah</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;16</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of the measure of <span class="key-term">onaah</span> being a sixth: less than a sixth is forgiven; more than a sixth, the sale is void; exactly a sixth &mdash; the transaction stands but the overcharge must be returned. For the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> <span class="bracket">[refinement]</span> is in the aspect of the six days of the workweek, which are the aspect of the six orders of the Mishnah, which are the aspect of permitted and forbidden, impure and pure, as is known. And during all six days of the workweek one must refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from the waste through commerce, which is the aspect of the thirty-nine <span class="key-term">melachos</span> <span class="bracket">[categories of work]</span>. And the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> is to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from the aspect of animal food, which was caused by the sin of Adam HaRishon, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the people went about and gathered&rdquo;</span> <span class="bracket">[<em>shatu ha&rsquo;am v&rsquo;laktu</em>]</span> &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;in folly&rdquo;</span> <span class="bracket">[<em>b&rsquo;shtusa</em>]</span>, which is said regarding the burdens of earning a livelihood during the six days of the workweek, as is brought elsewhere. For because during the weekdays there is a hold for the waste, which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> &mdash; the absence of <span class="key-term">daas</span> &mdash; therefore one who does not sanctify oneself properly can fall, God forbid, into folly, which is the deficiency of <span class="key-term">daas</span>, through the burden of earning a livelihood. And then one&rsquo;s livelihood comes with great toil, God forbid, for it is difficult for one to refine the livelihood that comes through the <span class="key-term">birur</span> of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above &mdash; because the deficiency of <span class="key-term">daas</span> and the folly that takes hold during the weekdays has taken hold of one. And this itself is drawn from the waste and the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> that were caused by the sin of Adam HaRishon, who fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore, <span class="verse">&ldquo;whoever presses the hour, the hour presses him.&rdquo;</span> For the more one exerts oneself after livelihood without trusting in Hashem &mdash; that He can sustain one through a minor cause &mdash; and one is not drawn after the true <span class="key-term">daas</span> to minimize business dealings and engage in Torah, therefore the hour presses him. For since one blemishes the <span class="key-term">daas</span>, one&rsquo;s livelihood comes with even more difficulty, for one cannot refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em>, from which the essential livelihood derives, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore, the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> during all the weekdays is through the holiness of Shabbos, for one must draw the holiness of Shabbos into the six days of the workweek, and then one merits to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em>. For the essential completeness of <span class="key-term">daas</span> is on Shabbos, as is known. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Remember the day of Shabbos to sanctify it&rdquo;</span> &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;remember it from the first day of the week.&rdquo;</span> And adjacent to it: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Six days you shall labor.&rdquo;</span> For through remembering Shabbos from the first day of the week &mdash; through which one draws the holiness of Shabbos into the six days of the workweek &mdash; through this, <span class="verse">&ldquo;six days you shall labor and do all your work.&rdquo;</span> For through this one can engage in one&rsquo;s work properly, for one can refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em> by drawing the holiness of Shabbos into the weekdays, through which one draws the <span class="key-term">daas</span> from Shabbos into the weekdays, through which the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em> is accomplished, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore we were commanded regarding the resting of one&rsquo;s animal on Shabbos, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;In order that your ox and your donkey may rest, like you&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Exodus 23:12]</span>. For during the weekdays, when there is a hold for the sin of Adam HaRishon &mdash; who blemished the <span class="key-term">daas</span> and fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, and then the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of the <em>behemah</em> is diminished, as mentioned above &mdash; therefore the <em>behemah</em> also has no rest. Therefore man and the <em>behemah</em> must toil and exert themselves in the thirty-nine <span class="key-term">melachos</span> in order to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> &mdash; so that the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> is refined for <em>adam</em>, and the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> for <em>behemah</em>. This is the aspect of the general principle of all the <span class="key-term">melachos</span> during the weekdays: to refine the grain from the chaff and straw, etc., in the physical and spiritual realms, as mentioned above. But on Shabbos, when the <span class="key-term">birur</span> is completed and the <span class="key-term">daas</span> of the person is perfected in completeness &mdash; for the essential rectification of the sin of Adam HaRishon is on Shabbos, for <span class="verse">&ldquo;Shabbos protects him&rdquo;</span> <span class="bracket">[<em>Shabbas agin alohee</em>]</span> &mdash; therefore on Shabbos the person leaves the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> and returns to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> in completeness. Therefore it is a great mitzvah to eat on Shabbos and to have abundant meals, for then one is nourished from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, which is the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <span class="key-term">daas</span> in completeness, pure and radiant, without waste &mdash; through which <span class="key-term">shefa</span> one merits a complete <span class="key-term">daas</span> to know and recognize Him, blessed be He.</p>

<p>Therefore, on Shabbos one must give rest to the <em>behemah</em> as well. For it certainly has rest now, since its sustenance has been fully restored to it, for man does not take any of its sustenance now, as mentioned above. And now how sweet to the palate are the words of our Sages, of blessed memory, who said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Give it rest, so that it may graze and eat,&rdquo;</span> etc. For certainly this is the essential mitzvah of the resting of one&rsquo;s animal: that it should do no work, and it should graze and eat its food and sustenance &mdash; for now its sustenance has been fully restored to it, since man is not drawing or taking from its sustenance at all, as mentioned above. And this is the essential rectification of the sin of Adam HaRishon: to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> for <em>behemah</em>, and the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> for <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, through which the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> is drawn, as mentioned above. For on Shabbos the <span class="key-term">sukkas shalom</span> <span class="bracket">[booth of peace]</span> is spread over us, as we bless on the eve of Shabbos: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Who spreads the <em>sukkas shalom</em> over us,&rdquo;</span> etc. And through this the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> during all the weekdays is accomplished &mdash; by drawing from Shabbos the aspect of the <span class="key-term">sukkas shalom</span> upon all the weekdays.</p>

<p>Therefore, during all the weekdays we pray in the blessing of <span class="key-term">Hashkiveinu</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And spread over us the <em>sukkah</em> of Your peace, and direct us with good counsel from before You.&rdquo;</span> For during all the weekdays one must draw the aspect of the holiness of the <span class="key-term">sukkas shalom</span> from Shabbos &mdash; when the <span class="key-term">sukkas shalom</span> is spread over us, etc. &mdash; through which the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em> is accomplished, as mentioned above, and through which the essential drawing of livelihood through all commerce and <span class="key-term">melachos</span> is accomplished, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is why <span class="verse">&ldquo;and direct us with good counsel from before You&rdquo;</span> is placed adjacent to <span class="verse">&ldquo;and spread over us the <em>sukkah</em> of Your peace.&rdquo;</span> For the essential drawing of wealth and livelihood through commerce is through good counsel. For if one would merit to know the right counsel in commerce &mdash; what to buy and trade &mdash; one would certainly always profit greatly, for there is certainly no time or season when there is not some merchandise through which one could become very wealthy. Only it has been decreed that <span class="verse">&ldquo;a person does not know in what he will profit.&rdquo;</span> And when Hashem, blessed be He, wishes to give livelihood or wealth to a person, He places good counsel in one&rsquo;s heart &mdash; what to trade &mdash; and through this one profits easily. And this is clear to anyone with a brain in his head (and as is explained elsewhere).</p>

<p>And this is what is written regarding commerce, that a person should not err, God forbid, to say: <span class="verse">&ldquo;My power and the might of my hand have made for me this wealth&rdquo;</span> &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;And you shall remember Hashem your God, for He is the One Who gives you power to make wealth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Deuteronomy 8:17&ndash;18]</span>. And the Targum renders: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For He is the One Who gives you counsel to acquire possessions.&rdquo;</span> For the essential wealth and livelihood is through counsel. Therefore, in truth, all the excess exertions and toils and worries and burdens and sadness that many people have regarding livelihood are all folly, vanity, and utter foolishness, for they do not help at all &mdash; on the contrary, they cause great harm. And the essential lack of livelihood comes from the excess of worries and burdens, for no exertion, toil, cleverness, or stratagem will help at all as long as one does not merit to know the complete counsel in commerce, as mentioned above. Therefore one need only raise one&rsquo;s eyes to heaven at all times, every day, and request mercy from the One Whose business it is &mdash; that He give one good counsel in one&rsquo;s heart, to know what to trade and how to conduct oneself in commerce &mdash; and then one&rsquo;s livelihood will come easily, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And the essential good counsel is drawn from the <span class="key-term">daas</span> that one merits through the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;if you call to <em>binah</em>,&rdquo;</span> through which the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> is accomplished and from which the essential livelihood derives, as mentioned above. Therefore <span class="verse">&ldquo;and direct us with good counsel&rdquo;</span> is placed adjacent to <span class="verse">&ldquo;and spread over us the <em>sukkah</em> of Your peace,&rdquo;</span> for through the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">daas</span>, one merits good counsel, from which the essential livelihood derives, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore, on the festival <span class="bracket">[of Sukkos]</span> we are judged regarding water. For the essential livelihood is drawn through water, through which all things grow. Therefore on the festival of Sukkos we are judged regarding this, for we need to draw livelihood through the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, through which one merits the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, as mentioned above &mdash; for the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> is through the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">daas</span>, as mentioned above. For <span class="verse">&ldquo;everything is refined through thought&rdquo;</span> <span class="bracket">[<em>kulla b&rsquo;machshavah isbariru</em>]</span>.</p>

<p>For the <span class="key-term">sukkah</span> is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Ananai Kavod</span> <span class="bracket">[Clouds of Glory]</span> that went before the children of Yisrael in the wilderness, and the <span class="key-term">Ananai Kavod</span> would kill the snakes and scorpions of the wilderness and straighten the way, as our Sages said, and as is brought in Rashi&rsquo;s commentary. For when one goes out to the marketplace to engage in external occupations &mdash; in commerce and the thirty-nine <span class="key-term">melachos</span> &mdash; it is like going in a wilderness full of snakes and scorpions, and one needs great protection so as not to stumble through them, God forbid. And the essential protection is through the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, which is a great protection. Therefore we request <span class="verse">&ldquo;and spread the <em>sukkah</em> of peace&rdquo;</span> in the blessing of <span class="key-term">Hashkiveinu</span>, which is the blessing of protection, as we conclude on the weekdays: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Who guards His people Yisrael forever.&rdquo;</span> And the essential protection is through the aspect of the spreading of the <span class="key-term">sukkas shalom</span> that is spread on Shabbos, from which the protection is drawn upon all the weekdays. For from the aspect of <span class="key-term">sukkah</span>, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Ananai Kavod</span> is drawn upon a person, going before him to straighten the way and to kill and destroy all the snakes and scorpions, etc. &mdash; which are the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> and waste that surround livelihood and wealth.</p>

<p>Therefore, when one goes out to the marketplace to engage in commerce, one must be especially careful to remember the Shabbos at all times, and to intend during the commerce to merit to receive the Shabbos properly and to select a fine portion for Shabbos, as our Sages said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Remember it from the first day of the week.&rdquo;</span> And when one remembers the Shabbos &mdash; which is the totality of the entire Torah &mdash; the holiness of the <span class="key-term">daas</span> of Shabbos will be drawn upon one, which is the aspect of the holiness of the <span class="key-term">sukkas shalom</span> that is spread on Shabbos. And through this one will not be bound up after physical money, but will remember at every turn one&rsquo;s end and purpose &mdash; that neither silver nor gold accompany a person, etc., but only Torah and good deeds alone. And one will direct all one&rsquo;s aspiration toward Torah and service of Hashem, and increase in <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span>, and minimize business dealings and engage in Torah, and trust in Hashem that all one&rsquo;s livelihood is only from Hashem, blessed be He, through the good counsel He will give one. And if Hashem, blessed be He, wishes to send one good counsel in one&rsquo;s heart, one will easily profit greatly; and if, God forbid, Hashem, blessed be He, does not wish to counsel one in what to profit, then no exertions or worries will help at all. And when one conducts commerce in this manner, then it is said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The toil of your hands you shall eat &mdash; you are praiseworthy, and it is good for you&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Psalms 128:2]</span>.</p>

<h3>&sect;17</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;You shall not muzzle an ox while it is threshing&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Deuteronomy 25:4]</span>, and we derive <span class="verse">&ldquo;ox&rdquo;</span> <span class="verse">&ldquo;ox&rdquo;</span> from Shabbos, etc. For at the time the ox is engaged in the work of threshing and the like, it is refining the wheat from the waste &mdash; that is, refining the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>. Therefore it certainly follows that one should not muzzle it then &mdash; not prevent it from its sustenance and eating &mdash; since our entire occupation with it in the work is for the purpose of this <span class="key-term">birur</span>: that is, to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span>, as mentioned above, and to restore to the <em>behemah</em> its sustenance, as mentioned above. Therefore one must allow it to eat as it wishes, since we are now engaged in restoring to it its sustenance and food and vitality, as mentioned above. Therefore we derive <span class="verse">&ldquo;ox&rdquo;</span> <span class="verse">&ldquo;ox&rdquo;</span> from Shabbos, where it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;In order that your ox may rest,&rdquo;</span> etc. For the prohibition of muzzling an ox while it is threshing and the mitzvah of the resting of one&rsquo;s animal are of one and the same aspect, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;18</h3>

<p class="no-indent">It turns out that the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em> to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em> during the weekdays is through the holiness of Shabbos that one draws into the weekdays, as mentioned above. Therefore the essential completion and perfection of the <span class="key-term">birur</span> is through the aspect of the sixth day, which is <span class="key-term">erev Shabbos Kodesh</span> <span class="bracket">[the eve of the holy Shabbos]</span>, when the additional holiness of Shabbos is drawn upon the weekdays. Then is the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;And it shall be on the sixth day, they shall prepare what they bring in&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Exodus 16:5]</span> &mdash; for then one refines and prepares the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> and the food from the weekday to Shabbos, which is the aspect of refining it from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em>. For the weekday in relation to Shabbos is in the aspect of <em>behemah</em> &mdash; the absence of <span class="key-term">daas</span> &mdash; in relation to <em>adam</em>, which is the <span class="key-term">daas</span>.</p>

<p>For Adam HaRishon was created on the sixth day. And our Sages said: in order that he enter the festive meal immediately. And then all the animals were also created. And immediately upon his creation, Hashem, blessed be He, said to him: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Behold, I have given you every herb&hellip; it shall be yours for food; and to every beast of the earth&hellip; every green herb for food&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Genesis 1:29&ndash;30]</span> &mdash; warning him immediately regarding his food and the food of the animals and beasts, that his food should be separate and the food of the animals should be separate. That is, that the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> and food of <em>adam</em> should not be mixed with the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> and food of <em>behemah</em>. But he did not fulfill the command of Hashem, blessed be He, and ate from the Tree of Knowledge, and through this he fell to the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>behemah</em>, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore we must refine through the thirty-nine <span class="key-term">melachos</span> during the six days of the workweek, as mentioned above. And therefore the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> is on the sixth day, when Adam was created and blemished then. And therefore then we must rectify &mdash; to refine the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em> &mdash; through the holiness of Shabbos, which is drawn then especially upon the person, as is known. Therefore the general term for the service of man in this world is called by the name <span class="key-term">erev Shabbos</span>, as our Sages said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Whoever toiled on <em>erev</em> Shabbos shall eat on Shabbos.&rdquo;</span> For the essential service is to refine the <span class="key-term">nitzozos</span> from the sin of Adam HaRishon &mdash; the essence of which is in the aspect of <span class="key-term">erev Shabbos</span>, which is the sixth day, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore Hashem added the <em>hei</em> to <span class="verse">&ldquo;<em>Ha</em>Shishi&rdquo;</span> <span class="bracket">[&ldquo;the sixth&rdquo;]</span>, to indicate that the entire world is suspended until the sixth of Sivan, when Yisrael received the five <span class="bracket">[<em>chamisha</em>]</span> books of the Torah. For the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> is through the Torah. Therefore the <em>hei</em> &mdash; which alludes to the Torah &mdash; was added specifically to <span class="verse">&ldquo;the sixth,&rdquo;</span> for the essential completeness of the <span class="key-term">birur</span> is on the sixth day, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3>&sect;19</h3>

<p class="no-indent">Therefore the measure of <span class="key-term">onaah</span> is a sixth &mdash; that is, one part in six &mdash; for the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> of commerce from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em> is in the aspect of the six days of activity, as mentioned above, and the essence is the sixth &mdash; that is, the sixth day, as mentioned above. Therefore when the <span class="key-term">onaah</span> is exactly a sixth: the transaction stands and the overcharge is returned. For as long as one has not blemished the <span class="key-term">daas</span> more than a sixth &mdash; which is one part in six, the aspect of the sixth day &mdash; there is still a remedy through return. And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span>: that one can return and restore the matter to its place. For the essential <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span> is in the aspect of the sixth day, when one elevates and returns the six days of the workweek into the holiness of Shabbos, which is the aspect of the World to Come. For the sixth day, on which Adam HaRishon was created, is in the aspect of Rosh HaShanah &mdash; for Adam HaRishon was created on Rosh HaShanah, as our Sages said &mdash; and Rosh HaShanah is the first day of <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span>. For the sixth day is the essential <span class="key-term">birur</span> from the contamination of the serpent, as mentioned above &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span>, in which one returns and rectifies the sin of Adam HaRishon, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore, as long as the <span class="key-term">onaah</span> is only a sixth, the transaction stands and the overcharge is returned, for there the remedy through return exists &mdash; for there is the essential <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span>, as mentioned above. But more than a sixth &mdash; the sale is void. For when one has distanced oneself more than a sixth and has completely departed from the aspect of the sixth day, then one cannot refine, and the transaction is completely void. But less than a sixth is forgiven, for less than a sixth begins to enter into the aspect of one-seventh. And there, forgiveness is granted through the holiness of Shabbos, which is on the seventh day &mdash; on which sins are forgiven, as our Sages said on the verse: <span class="verse">&ldquo;<em>mechallelo</em>&rdquo;</span> &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;it is forgiven for him&rdquo;</span> <span class="bracket">[<em>machul lo</em>]</span>.</p>

<p class="section-note"><span class="bracket">(This pertains to the above.)</span></p>

<h3>&sect;20</h3>

<p class="no-indent">This is the aspect of what our Sages said: it is forbidden for a person to eat before feeding one&rsquo;s animal, as it is said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And I will give grass in your field for your cattle&rdquo;</span> &mdash; and afterward: <span class="verse">&ldquo;and you shall eat and be satisfied&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">[Deuteronomy 11:15]</span>. For certainly one must feed one&rsquo;s animal first, before eating oneself, in order to restore and give the food and <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of the <em>behemah</em> to the <em>behemah</em> &mdash; to demonstrate that one has no hold, God forbid, in the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of the <em>behemos</em>. For one restores to it its sustenance and gives it its food first, before eating oneself. And then, precisely, one may eat oneself &mdash; for now one is nourished from the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of <em>adam</em>, since one has already restored the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of the <em>behemah</em> to the <em>behemah</em> by fulfilling the mitzvah of the Torah and giving the <em>behemah</em> its food first, as mentioned above.</p>

<p class="section-note"><span class="bracket">(Halachah 5 &mdash; in Hilchos Sheluchim, Halachah 5, &sect;14.)</span></p>

<!-- TRANSLATOR'S SUMMARY FOR MU4 -->

<div class="summary-box">
<h4>&#x1F4D6; Translator&rsquo;s Summary</h4>

<p><strong>Mekach Umimkar 4</strong> is based on Likutay Moharan I:266 (<em>&ldquo;And for his cattle he made sukkos&rdquo;</em>). Its central theme: the distinction between the <em>shefa</em> (influx/sustenance) of <em>adam</em> (man) and the <em>shefa</em> of <em>behemah</em> (animal). The sin of Adam HaRishon caused man to fall from the human level of sustenance to the animalistic level. The rectification comes through the <em>sukkah</em>, which is the aspect of <em>Binah</em> (Understanding) &mdash; &ldquo;<em>Ima</em> who shelters over her children.&rdquo;</p>

<p>The patriarchs were shepherds precisely to restore animal sustenance to the animals and draw only human sustenance for themselves. Dovid HaMelech, as the seventh shepherd, completed this rectification, which is why the <em>sukkah</em> bears his name. His opposite, Nevuchadnetzar, who destroyed the Temple, was punished by becoming an animal for seven years &mdash; corresponding to the Seven Shepherds he damaged.</p>

<p>Commerce exists to refine the sparks from the animal level to the human level. Therefore: transactions are not finalized through words alone (everything was created through utterance = animal level), but through acts of the hands (man was created by the Hand = human level = <em>sukkah</em>). <em>Kinyan sudar</em> works because garments = Clouds of Glory = <em>sukkah</em>. The house acquires because the house derives from <em>sukkah</em>. Priestly gifts, <em>tzedakah</em>, and <em>maaser sheini</em> all refine sustenance from <em>behemah</em> to <em>adam</em> through the power of <em>sukkah</em>.</p>

<p>The sub-section on <em>Hilchos Onaah</em> (&sect;&sect;15&ndash;20) extends the teaching: fraud (<em>onaah</em>) blemishes the <em>daas</em> and prevents the refinement. The measure of <em>onaah</em> is one-sixth, corresponding to the six workdays through which the <em>birur</em> is accomplished. The essential refinement depends on drawing Shabbos holiness into the weekdays; Shabbos is when the <em>sukkas shalom</em> is spread over us, restoring all sustenance to its proper place. Good counsel (<em>eitzah tovah</em>) in commerce comes from <em>daas</em> drawn through <em>sukkah</em>. Not muzzling the ox during threshing, feeding one&rsquo;s animal before eating, and the holiness of the sixth day all express the same principle of restoring the <em>shefa</em> of <em>behemah</em> to <em>behemah</em> and the <em>shefa</em> of <em>adam</em> to <em>adam</em>.</p>
</div>

